{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/adr/*.md'","aggregated_output":"# 1. Native operation authority owns coordination\n\nDate: 2026-10-16. Status: selected following owner candidate selection; independent G01 verdict\nand implementation readiness are tracked in planning/status.md. Implements D008,D009,D013,D014,D016,D019.\n\nV1 already has deep domain/request modules, but GPUI callers still coordinate\nslots, protected-key IO and ordered effects. React must not inherit that authority.\n\nChoose a principal-bound Rust actor with dispatch(Intent) and observe(ViewScope).\nKeep feature transitions domain-owned inside one initial core crate. Native\nbootstrap injects adapters and creates operator/Harness handles; JSON cannot\nselect the caller principal. Finite domain instructions exclude arbitrary SDK\nmethod strings and any Harness Apply capability.\n\nThe interface includes atomic admission/context retirement, per-source supersession,\nseparate read/review/write/stream domains, priority/deadline/rate-limit semantics,\nbounded queues, bounded delivery-sequence deduplication with safe session rotation,\nsingle-use settlement and truthful Remote outcome. No remote IO\nor blocking vault call occurs while the authoritative transition is locked.\nAdmitted work runs on the host's one async runtime; native adapters execute effects.\n\nReact owns raw editor text/undo. Rust owns immutable captured drafts/reviews.\nReview/Apply/Save/Send capture fresh input in their actual production handlers;\nApply compares fresh input with the stored reviewed operation and executes only\nthat stored operation. Invalid/lossy input, changed context/draft/resource or a\nconsumed review refuses dispatch. Never rely only on a debounced revision.\nRequestApply uses a native operator confirmation; actual Apply completion is\nprivate, single-use and revalidated after the modal editor/context lease.\nEvery scoped intent/observation carries native-issued context and principal\nadmission. Async vault completions are generation/lease-bound; obsolete writes\nreceive orphan cleanup rather than reactivating credentials. Explicit one-time\nsecret reveal/copy stays in a scoped transient native dialog, never snapshots.\n\nAlternatives considered under the design-it-twice skill:\n\n| Design | Depth/locality | Cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| Actor dispatch/observe | Callers learn one authority seam; context and settlement stay together | Finite unions and observation backpressure need discipline |\n| Typed scoped handles | Strong domain methods and revoked scopes; flexible internal composition | More handles/methods and IPC registries for callers to coordinate |\n| Task-oriented scan board | Trivial first scan workflow | Public task surface grows across all parity features |\n\nRecommend the actor with domain-specific types and a small generated presentation\nfacade. Retain the alternatives' explicit scoped validation and effortless scan\nusage internally. Do not combine all their public surfaces or add pass-through\nmodules merely to obtain two method names.\n\nTwo real execution adapters (SDK/scripted), storage adapters (Keychain/session/\nfault-injectable) and clocks justify internal seams. The interface is the test\nsurface: switch/replace/cancel while queued/dispatched, old/duplicate reply,\nfresh-input races, double Apply, denied Harness Apply, unknown outcome/no replay,\npriority/deadline/rate-limit containment and observation resynchronization.\n\nSee [selected design](../architecture/DESIGN.md) for ownership/wire details.\nNo app code has been written and no native/SDK test is claimed by this ADR.\n# 2. Share Academy presentation through explicit composition\n\nDate: 2026-10-16. Status: selected following owner candidate selection; independent G01 verdict\nand implementation readiness are tracked in planning/status.md. Implements D004,D005,D006,D007,D010.\n\nThe current UI package re-exports web app source. Shell palette/mobile navigation\nand theme persistence require tRPC/Clerk/router context; the authenticated web\nentry also starts learner and manager behavior. A whole-app import would spread\nthat authority into unrelated desktop features.\n\nKeep one Academy-owned presentation implementation. Create explicit provider-free\ncontrols/theme/shell exports while preserving the existing tooling entry. Both\nAcademy web and desktop consume the extracted source. Composition adapters supply\nbrand/navigation/account/header/palette/mobile slots; the shared module owns\nvisual semantics, responsive layout and focus. No universal plugin framework.\n\nDesktop global theme is an app preference stored through Rust, not hosted\nsettings.update. Academy web keeps its learner-account theme behavior. Learner\nnotifications, gamification and account effects mount only in Academy composition.\n\nExtract learner views separately when C05/C06 require them. Retain React Query/\ntRPC hooks behind a transport/navigation provider; type-only learner contracts\nbuild without the Express/DB runtime. Web uses existing HTTP authentication;\ndesktop uses a terminating link into the allowlisted Rust Academy transport.\nTokens stay native. Hosted learning/access/grading/award truth and client-safe\nbundle/draft contracts remain authoritative. Never bundle raw answer content.\n\nDirectly embedding the authenticated web root is rejected because its interface\ncontains unrelated account/manager assumptions. Maintaining a desktop UI copy\nis rejected because appearance and learner behavior would diverge.\n\nTests render shared presentation without hosted identity/query providers, run\nboth consumers' regressions, verify native keyboard/focus/themes, and prove no\nlearner mutation/gamification effect from general desktop screens. Learner tests\ncover native link envelopes/allowlist, account cache retirement and hosted authority.\n\nDependency/source/license pins are extraction prerequisites. This ADR changes\nno Academy checkout, package or hosted registration. See\n[selected design](../architecture/DESIGN.md).\n# 3. Retain native Harness and own scoped identity in Rust\n\nDate: 2026-10-16. Status: selected following owner candidate selection; independent G01 verdict\nand implementation readiness are tracked in planning/status.md. Implements D010,D011,D014–D016,D021–D023.\n\nDesktop-server is already a Rust engine. V1 host workers and its package manifest\nstill require Node/managed CLI. Preserve engine depth and replace those host\nrequirements, rather than rewrite the agent. Source inspection alone does not\nestablish that a newly sealed installed bundle works without the old resources.\n\nNative lifecycle owns sealed executable selection, bounded stdin bootstrap,\nprotocol supervision, process cleanup, scoped grants and protected history.\nReact only presents lifecycle state. Grant/tenant/project changes retire the\nrun; approvals bind actual call items. Preserve existing project/process/tool\nrestrictions, Gateway-only inference/MCP and no engine Apply.\n\nIdentity shares native discovery/HTTP/validation/storage mechanics while retaining\nAcademy learner, Harness inference and MCP grant policies. They are distinct\nidentities with distinct sign-out/refresh/context effects. Use public-client\nPKCE/device flows and a no-redirect native transport; never embed a client secret\nor trust renderer-selected issuer/token destinations.\n\nHost signature/JWKS validation is a deliberate stricter v2 requirement; v1\nomitted it. Validate ID/access token types according to their actual contracts,\nnot by decoding arbitrary JWT claims. Rotation/expiry/sleep/revocation fail closed.\nSame-identity token refresh restarts the one-shot-bootstrap engine and restores\ncompatible in-session history; it re-confirms workspace-write permission and\nnever replays remote/tool effects. Declining workspace-write confirmation keeps\nthe draft/cancels Send without restart. Any changed ContextBinding (including\nlocal access/model/configuration/MCP inventory) starts a new conversation; its\nold history is inspect-only under the new binding. MCP-only token rotation also\nrebootstraps/restores an identical binding, but retains working v1's current\nproject-access confirmation without an SSO refresh or another write prompt.\nNative scope additionally binds per-server MCP grant IDs/catalog revisions absent\nfrom engine equality; re-sign-in/sign-out/removal/revision change retires the\nconversation. Expiry alone leaves inference usable with that non-required server\nunavailable and native calls denied. This continuity is distinct from inspect-only\nimported history. No token or refresh credential enters React, diagnostics, process arguments or\ninherited environment. One-time operator-entered inputs remain transient.\n\nUse independent v2 bundle/data/Keychain namespaces. Protected work is encrypted\nand account/context-scoped; no plaintext fallback. Reviewed import creates a new\nv2 data generation, never modifies v1, transfers no credentials/approvals and\nretains a restartable receipt/rollback generation. Historical conversations are\ninspect-only until fresh-context compatibility is qualified.\n\nTests cross native process and identity interfaces: malformed/oversized bootstrap,\nqueue pressure, wrong context, crash/EOF/graceful and forced cleanup, signature/\nissuer/audience/key-rotation rejection, scoped sign-out, protected histories and\nNode-free installed inventory. Native/live/final signed-byte proof remain separate.\nSee [selected design](../architecture/DESIGN.md) for identity/crypto proposals.\n# 4. Managed HTTP enters native configuration authority\n\nDate: 2026-10-16. Status: selected following owner candidate selection; independent G01 verdict\nand implementation readiness are tracked in planning/status.md. Implements D014,D016 and C14/C15 requirements.\n\nV1's workbench has real request-document and transport depth. Its redactions-based\nredirect guard is not explicit tenant-credential classification, Live mode lacks\napplication destination binding, and its post-401 retry can resend a mutation.\nThe stricter v2 review/no-replay policy must be enforced below every Send path.\n\nKeep RequestDocument reconciliation separate. Native execution admission captures\na fresh immutable effective request and explicitly distinguishes tenant-managed,\nworkbench-owned and anonymous credentials. Known managed reads need capability/\ndestination admission. Known mutations need exact Configuration review. Unknown\nmanaged methods/paths are denied, even if presented as a read or generic draft.\nOrdinary workbench-owned/anonymous HTTP remains supported.\n\nReplace the editable SCM collection-ID credential gate with native-owned\ncapability registration. Imported IDs/references cannot authorize tenant secret\nresolution. An edited token_url/request URL is admitted against the explicit\ncredential destination before secrets are obtained; an ID change never creates\na capability. Preserve operator-reviewed endpoint configuration separately.\n\nBind review to expanded URL/method/headers/body and file hashes, variables,\ncookies, credential/context/destination and resource classification. Recheck\nbefore dispatch; changed input/context/files require fresh review. Rust constructs\nthe actual request; renderer fields cannot mark it preapproved.\n\nManaged redirects are disabled initially: a 3xx is shown, and following it is a\nnew prepared/admitted request. Generic redirects preserve bounded cookie/credential\norigin policy. No automatic workbench resend follows HTTP401, refresh, reconnect,\nlost response, import or history replay. Refresh can precede a new explicit Send.\n\nThe built-in catalogue has 193 request specifications, 81 with mutation methods;\nthis is metadata parity, not a claim of dedicated/live-qualified product support.\nTests cover imported/edited requests, unknown managed endpoints, direct IPC bypass,\nambiguous paths/auth headers, same/cross-origin redirects, stale cookie/file/\nvariable/context bindings, double Apply and post-401/lost-response no resend.\n\nThis is a stricter v2 product contract, not an allegation that v1 failed its own\ncontract. See [selected design](../architecture/DESIGN.md).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
