{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/planning/IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md docs/planning/dependencies.md docs/planning/parity-matrix.md'","aggregated_output":"# Prisma AIRS Desktop v2 implementation plan\n\nStatus: product interview decisions D001–D023 accepted; D024/D025 settle source\nterms and all four architecture candidates; D026 makes Codex the independent\nchunk and phase reviewer. G00/G01 passed; implementation proceeds from C01. A passing plan review is not a passing architecture,\nSDK, application, live-tenant, or package review.\n\n## Outcome and exclusions\n\nDeliver a fresh macOS Apple Silicon desktop application with React presentation\nin Tauri, a focused Rust application core, direct Rust SCM SDK integration, and\nthe native Rust Harness engine. Academy supplies shared presentation and remains\nthe authority for remote learning. Preserve agreed working v1 behavior, using\nv1 as requirements reference. Do not translate its GPUI implementation wholesale.\n\nNo desktop billing, media-generation backend, local MySQL/Redis server stack,\nNode/Bun backend runtime, TypeScript workers, speculative browser client, or\nin-app updater is included. Academy gamification remains inside Academy. Gateway\nusage/cost/budget/limits remain operational product functionality. Build-time\nJavaScript tooling and React WebView JavaScript are expected.\n\nSource destination: `ssh://git@git-ssh.cdot.io/cdot/prisma-airs-desktop-v2.git`.\nCheckout: `/Users/cdot/development/redtail/prisma-airs-desktop-v2`.\n\n## Architectural guiding principles\n\n1. Design deep modules: substantial behavior behind a small domain interface.\n   Apply the deletion test; do not wrap every SDK method in a pass-through module.\n2. The interface is the test surface. Exercise production transitions and\n   adapters; use independent wire/protocol expectations for external contracts.\n3. One adapter is a hypothetical seam; two real adapters justify a seam. Shared\n   Academy presentation has real web/desktop consumers. Do not build speculative\n   browser/backend/plugin architectures for this desktop delivery.\n4. Rust owns authority and locality for tenant/credential/workspace context,\n   request lifecycle, configuration review, protected storage, and approvals.\n   React owns presentation and editable input, not permission to execute.\n5. The SDK owns its declared transport/authentication contracts. The application\n   owns interactive identity, OS storage, context admission, and workflow policy.\n   Do not duplicate SDK retry/pagination/OAuth policy without a documented need.\n6. Unknown outcomes and partial/stale/denied/unsupported data remain distinct.\n   Never map an unknown verdict to allow or a cancelled write to successful rollback.\n7. Host credentials and capabilities are explicit. No ambient environment-file\n   discovery, inherited production fallback, generic renderer secret access,\n   unrestricted native plugin grants, or cross-origin credential forwarding.\n8. Shared appearance does not imply shared learner state. Tenant operations,\n   Academy identity/progression, Harness inference identity, and MCP grants stay\n   separately scoped. A tenant switch does not sign the learner out of Academy.\n9. Keep provenance and reproducibility local to dependency selection. Exact\n   versions, source hashes, build inputs, notices, and protocol pins are evidence;\n   a neighboring active worktree is not a release dependency.\n10. Measure native usability/performance and the actual installed package. A\n    successful browser render or mocked IPC assertion is insufficient evidence\n    for Tauri host behavior, VoiceOver, Keychain, sidecar isolation, or notarization.\n\nConcrete interfaces, crate decomposition, shared package extraction, and storage\nformats are outputs of G01. This plan defines behavior and testable work, not\nunreviewed Rust signatures or a predetermined hierarchy of tiny modules.\n\n## Ordered phases and chunks\n\nEvery Cxx has its own instruction file under [chunks](chunks/README.md). Complete\nchunks in numeric order. A dependency delay blocks its chunk; report it honestly\nand continue only research/preparation explicitly within that chunk. Do not\nsilently advance a later phase or replace a real dependency with a fake to pass.\nFor a prolonged upstream stall, report the exact dependency and offer an owner\nreorder/scope decision. Do not wait indefinitely or reorder silently; an approved\nchange updates predecessors, plan and review evidence before execution.\n\n| Phase | Chunks   | Result                                                           |\n|-------|----------|------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| P00   | G00, G01 | Confirmed plan; selected and reviewed architecture               |\n| P01   | C01–C03  | Shared desktop shell, native core, first complete Runtime scan   |\n| P02   | C04–C07  | Academy identity, learner presentation, assessment, offline work |\n| P03   | C08–C12  | Runtime/DLP administration, Sessions, reports, Library           |\n| P04   | C13–C15  | Existing Red Team/Model reads and complete API Client workflows  |\n| P05   | C16–C18  | Gateway workspace/configuration, reviewed changes, inference     |\n| P06   | C19–C22  | Native Harness, Rust sign-in, typed host tools, workspace MCP    |\n| P07   | C23–C24  | Reviewed imports, native quality, accessibility/privacy closure  |\n| P08   | C25–C26  | Controlled live qualification; signed installed DMG acceptance   |\n| P09   | C27–C44  | UI v2 \"Refined Native\": spec, shell, wizard, destinations (D058); re-cut from C35 as one screen per chunk ported from the prototype (D059) |\n\n### G00 — Plan confirmation\n\nFinish the decision ledger, baseline coverage, chunk instructions, review/test\nprotocols, dependency gates, and architecture handoff. Obtain an actual independent\nplan review meeting D019. Product decisions are accepted and the owner explicitly\nselected the architecture candidates and source terms in D024/D025. Continue the\nrequested design work; no further blanket scope question is needed. Architecture\nreview and implementation evidence remain distinct gates.\n\n### G01 — Architecture improvement workflow\n\nFollow [the handoff](architecture-handoff.md) and the requested\nimprove-codebase-architecture skill. Explore the named areas, show a temporary\nHTML report with before/after candidates, ask the owner to choose, and grill the\nselected design. Produce ADRs, interface/test ownership, dependency/import\ndecisions, and concrete chunk command specifications. Review the architecture\nat least 9/10 in every critical dimension and overall. Revise this plan if the\nselected design affects it, then re-review affected planning evidence.\n\nNo application scaffolding, shared-source refactoring, real-data migration,\nproduct endpoint calls, or packaging implementation begins before G01 passes.\n\n## Per-chunk execution contract\n\n1. Read AGENTS/CLAUDE, glossary, accepted ADRs, the chunk, predecessor receipts,\n   dependency manifest, test catalogue, and its canonical implementer prompt.\n2. Confirm a clean approved source snapshot and identify unrelated user work.\n   Resolve dependency availability/provenance and baseline check limitations.\n3. Implement only that chunk and approved supporting changes. A shared Academy,\n   SDK, or Harness change needs its own reviewed revision and regression evidence;\n   preserve active work and do not move another project's main branch casually.\n4. Run exact checks from the approved command manifest. Use deterministic local\n   fixtures and literal external contracts, then the appropriate native tests.\n   Never call hosted application endpoints by accident.\n5. Record commands, environments, inputs, results, failures, hashes, limitations,\n   and rollback rehearsal. Save raw sensitive evidence privately; commit redacted\n   summaries with references/hashes, not credentials or customer bodies.\n6. Freeze source and dependency inputs. Request actual independent Codex\n   review through [the independent prompt](prompts/review-chunk.md) (D026).\n7. If any critical dimension/overall score is below 9, required fixes remain,\n   source changed, or mandatory evidence is absent: remediate, rerun affected\n   checks, freeze a new snapshot, and request a new review of the same chunk.\n8. Complete only after the receipt and evidence validate against current inputs.\n   After a phase's last chunk, obtain the cumulative Codex phase review\n   ([prompt](prompts/review-phase.md)) before starting the next phase.\n   Make a focused commit; revalidate that its tree matches the reviewed tree.\n   Later edits invalidate affected receipts and trigger targeted regression\n   checks/re-review. Preserve failed attempts; never pressure a reviewer to pass.\n\n## Command contract to establish in C01\n\nThese commands are a required future interface, not tools that exist today:\n\n```text\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- check --chunk Cxx --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- test --chunk Cxx --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- native --chunk Cxx --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- review --chunk Cxx --reviewer codex --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- review --phase Pxx --reviewer codex --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- complete --chunk Cxx --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- package --kind preview --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\ncargo run --locked -p xtask -- package --kind release-candidate --manifest docs/architecture/checks.json\n```\n\nC01 creates the controller and a versioned manifest of exact commands, working\ndirectories, targets, features, fixtures, timeouts, and expected evidence. It\ncannot implement the later chunks itself. G01 specifies actual Rust/pnpm/Tauri\ncommands after choosing the workspace; a future engineer must not guess them or\nclaim these placeholder commands already ran. Document/test the controller's\nrejection of missing, stale, malformed, edited, or sub-threshold receipts.\n\n## Coverage and evidence\n\n- [Feature baseline](feature-baseline.md): existing working/preview/stub behavior.\n- [Parity matrix](parity-matrix.md): work ownership and release closure.\n- [Dependency gates](dependencies.md): accepted inputs and unresolved qualification.\n- [Test catalogue](test-catalogue.md): named behavioral/native/artifact test cases.\n- [Review protocol](review-protocol.md): scoring, receipt fields, invalidation.\n- [Release contract](release-contract.md): live scope, signing, package/install proof.\n- [Mandatory live checks](live-checks.md): fixed L-family/F-smoke requirements and\n  owner-approved per-workflow live scope; no access-driven silent reductions.\n- [Distribution gate](distribution.md): owner-selected source/binary terms,\n  Academy permission, framework disposition and exact shipped notices.\n- [Status](status.md): authoritative current state; planned is not implemented.\n\nG01 must convert each chunk's named tests into exact invocation commands and\nobservable assertions. Tests cannot simply repeat implementation decisions.\nFresh signed-artifact checks bind the final DMG hash and installed bytes; source\nor fixture checks do not substitute for them.\n\n## Expected sequencing dependencies\n\nThe scan proof can use accepted SDK Phase 3 after native macOS qualification.\nManagement/DLP uses accepted Phase 4 or a later explicitly reviewed compatible\npin. Existing Red Team/Model reads need verified Phase 5 capabilities; complete\nGateway needs Phase 6 capabilities. Harness/Academy transports are application\nwork, not delivered by the SCM SDK. Keep these upstream dependencies visible and\ndo not require unrelated SDK operations merely because they share a library.\n\nFirst-slice metrics establish named budgets before C04. Every UI chunk includes\nkeyboard/focus checks. Later introducing chunks register their numeric workload\nbudgets before implementation/acceptance measurement under T20 governance; budget\nchanges need recorded rationale and owner or independent reviewer acknowledgement.\nC24/C26 compare these pre-registered values, not newly fitted limits. C24 closes\nthe full native/VoiceOver/performance and cross-feature offline matrix.\nPreview packages may demonstrate accepted scope but must name missing features.\nOnly C26 can establish stable installed-package readiness.\n\n## Completion and delivery\n\nStable v2 requires every agreed working-v1 parity row closed, all chunk/phase\nreviews passing, designated live acceptance complete, no missing mandatory\nchecks, and C26's installed signed/notarized DMG evidence. V1 stays available;\nfresh credentials and reviewed imports remain explicit. Updates initially use\nmanual signed DMGs with rollback instructions.\n\nThe active implementation task may deliver reviewed Git commits to the exact\nowner-specified remote using normal pushes. Application release publication,\nhosting changes, and promotion over v1 must remain within the owner's explicit\nrelease instruction; preparing a signed package does not by itself publish it.\n# Dependency and source gates\n\nArchitecture proposed exact first-slice versions in docs/architecture/qualification.md.\nAs of C01 (2026-10-17) the desktop graph is resolved, locked and compiled on\nthe macOS ARM64 host; the resolved inputs are recorded below. Later SDK\nfamilies and other inputs remain gated at their consuming chunks.\n\n## Source ownership\n\n| Input          | Inspected revision                       | Ownership/use                                           |\n|----------------|------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------|\n| cdot-framework | e3553b27a3d6bf457a2e585c5ae479c7db89a17b | Selective patterns/modules after provenance evaluation  |\n| Desktop v1     | 74754c02b19d87187b6dca81f64550a669b0f841 | Behavioral/contracts reference; preserve checkout       |\n| Academy        | 7f3a28c4082a5bb278bbff5d79fab106c240155a | Shared React source; hosted learning authority          |\n| Native Harness | 9331a5839bc6a763d94dee7584746f58bbbe1181 | Desktop-capable native engine/protocol input            |\n| SDK Phase 3    | ec6230d2a19b9c835c9e4c9487795b38ad538af3 | Accepted scan subset; native/live qualification pending |\n| scm-sdk crate  | crates.io 0.1.0, sha256 6d555d955c3734dd5ee78f7173569bdecd4426095b2ffedc4b77d8f0f2c2e8d9, from 4f65dc48686a3b701ed0585812fcca46859f7e5a | D027 scan input from C02 (scan feature only); 164 package unit tests pass natively; live qualification is C25 |\n| SDK Phase 4    | 32cbcb6d9b04478aeca21e767ed6ddb8949ec7bb | Accepted management/DLP/IAM subset; qualify exact uses  |\n\nDo not consume an active neighboring worktree via an unpinned path and later\nclaim the accepted commit was built. Obtain a clean revision-specific source\nsnapshot/package without secrets or ignored local configuration. Manifest both\nits origin revision and actual source/package hash. A dependency update reopens\nthe affected contract/native/artifact checks and review. Never fabricate SDK\nmethod parity from a similar TypeScript method name.\n\n## C01 resolved inputs\n\nRecorded by C01 and bound to its review. Locks: `Cargo.lock`, `pnpm-lock.yaml`,\n`rust-toolchain.toml`, `docs/architecture/toolchain.json`,\n`docs/architecture/inputs.lock.json`; the controller's dependency fingerprint\nhashes them with the consumed `.inputs/` bytes and tool identities.\n\n| Input | Resolved | Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| Rust toolchain | 1.99.0 (b940084d7 2026-09-28) | Corrected from 1.90.0; proc-macro dylib dyld failure at deployment target 13.0 on macOS 27 (evidence/C01/toolchain-correction.json). Release `strip` removed for the same failure. |\n| Tauri / tauri-build / Tauri CLI / @tauri-apps/api | 2.12.4 / 2.7.3 / 2.12.3 / 2.12.4 | `custom-protocol` added by the Tauri CLI for bundles |\n| ts-rs | 12.0.1 (serde-compat, no-serde-warnings) | Generated declarations committed; `xtask bindings --check` |\n| React / ReactDOM | 19.2.3 | Single instance per consumer (pnpm strict peers) |\n| Tailwind / Vite / Vitest / plugin-react / TypeScript | 4.3.2 / 7.3.6 / 3.2.6 / 5.2.0 / 5.9.3 | Matched to Academy's resolved lock instead of the earlier 4.1.18 / 7.3.0 proposal |\n| Build Node / pnpm | 24.21.0 / 10.6.5 (corepack shim in `.tools/bin`) | Build-only; never shipped |\n| Academy shared presentation | `ai-security-academy` 891f65eef76b53eb87155d0f0f5622228e217a2d on branch `v2/desktop-presentation` (base 7f3a28c4) | Pushed to the Academy origin on 2026-10-17 (owner-approved; main untouched). `xtask fetch-inputs --source <academy clone>` materializes `.inputs/academy` (tree sha256 1c4ce702…); a fresh clone from origin reproduces it (evidence/C01/clean-checkout). |\n\nThird-party notices for the shipped graph are in `docs/architecture/notice-inventory.json`\n(`xtask notices --check`). The Academy package is Academy-owned and recorded by\nits pinned commit, not relicensed.\n\n## Required gates\n\n- **Distribution terms:** G01 records owner-approved v2 source/binary terms,\n  Academy redistribution permission and every framework-derived import's\n  disposition under [distribution.md](distribution.md). No extraction before\n  clearance; C26 verifies notices/terms against exact shipped inventory.\n\n- **Provenance:** evaluate each direct import's actual license/notice and allowed\n  usage. cdot-framework is not blanket MIT and its billing-retention condition\n  cannot be erased by renaming. Prefer independently implemented patterns where\n  direct copying is unsuitable. Academy sharing is owner-directed; establish\n  package ownership and third-party notices rather than inventing a license.\n- **Academy packaging:** React19/Tailwind4/Vite7 are observed in Academy, while\n  the framework uses React18/Tailwind3. Select a compatible pinned desktop stack\n  and one shared presentation source. The existing UI package re-exports app\n  source and is not a ready independently reusable full learner app.\n- **Shared-source changes:** propose the smallest extraction that supports actual\n  web/desktop consumers. Keep Academy web behavior and hosted contracts stable;\n  run both projects' affected tests. Pin the reviewed shared revision/package\n  before completing its consuming desktop chunk.\n- **SDK scan:** ec6230d2's accepted subset supplies synchronous scan. It requires\n  explicit scan credentials; management OAuth is separate. Accepted Linux\n  reports do not establish macOS ARM64 support. Qualify the native compiler/TLS\n  dependencies, runtime integration, scanner contracts, cancellation, sanitized\n  errors, and unknown outcomes in C02–C03.\n- **SDK administration:** 32cbcb6d's accepted Phase4 is a candidate input for\n  C08–C12. Map every actual operation, option, pagination bound, and error to\n  accepted source/tests. SDK family labels are insufficient proof of parity.\n- **SDK later families:** Phase5 Red Team/Model and Phase6 Gateway were developing\n  or pending during inspection. Their exact accepted pins are prerequisites to\n  C13/C16–C18. Do not consume unfinished work or substitute mocks as completion.\n  Stable v2 must qualify the SDK subset it actually uses, including native/live\n  evidence; it need not claim every unrelated SDK method is complete.\n- **Harness:** retain the desktop-capable native engine/protocol after source and\n  package checks. Do not substitute an older canonical checkout or npm launcher.\n  Rebuild/reseal v2 resources to omit Node/managed CLI where proven unnecessary;\n  old v1 resource hashes do not attest the changed v2 bundle. Preserve inference\n  and MCP routing/context/tool restrictions.\n- **Native host:** select pinned Tauri2/Rust/toolchain dependencies compatible\n  with macOS ARM64 and the chosen SDK. Resolve one application-owned async\n  runtime strategy; do not create an independent runtime per request.\n- **Identity:** specify independent v2 bundle/display/data/Keychain identities in\n  G01. Test v1/v2 coexistence, reset, uninstall, import, and rollback. Do not\n  silently reuse a v1 namespace or change the learner's remote account.\n- **Live environment:** identify designated test tenants/accounts, scopes,\n  reversible resources, budgets, and cleanup/readback before C25 execution.\n  Prod configuration discovery is not mutation authorization. Missing access is\n  a real dependency gap; never report skipped tests as passed.\n- **Hosted OAuth registrations:** G01 maps reuse/new-client/redirect/scope needs\n  for Academy device authorization, Harness company SSO and MCP. Responsible\n  Academy/Gateway/IdP operators own authorized staging/configuration changes and\n  deployment. V2 identity alone neither proves a new registration is required\n  nor authorizes production changes. Resolve before the consuming live tests.\n- **Signing:** identify an authorized Developer ID, provisioning/entitlement\n  requirements, notarization access, and a native acceptance host. Access secrets\n  only at use time through approved storage, never committed plan variables.\n\n## Official host references\n\nTauri supports Rust commands and async messages between presentation and host;\nthe selected command/module interface still requires G01 design and review.\n[Calling Rust](https://v2.tauri.app/develop/calling-rust/)\n\nWindow/WebView capability grants require deliberate scoping; renderer grants do\nnot replace Rust's application authority checks.\n[Capabilities](https://v2.tauri.app/security/capabilities/)\n\nDMG distribution and macOS signing are separate from successful compilation.\n[DMG packaging](https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/dmg/),\n[macOS signing/notarization](https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/sign/macos/).\n# Working-v1 parity and release closure\n\nAll v2 rows are **planned**. No v2 source/native/live/artifact result exists yet.\nThe baseline is [feature-baseline.md](feature-baseline.md); do not expand a\npreview/stub into required live behavior without an explicit scope decision.\n\n| Requirement family                     | Owning chunks   | Closure requirement                                                                  |\n|----------------------------------------|-----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Tenant setup/scan-only/protected state | C02,C03,C08,C23 | Context/capabilities, reviewed endpoint overrides/profile import, verification/reset |\n| Runtime synchronous scan/cases         | C03,C12         | Faithful verdicts, profiles, cancellation and no silent replay                       |\n| Profiles/topics/applications/keys      | C08,C09         | Exact supported reads/writes, review binding, one-time secrets                       |\n| DLP/deployment catalogue               | C08,C10         | Exact supported operation subset and real multipart semantics                        |\n| Sessions/content/search/cache          | C11             | Explicit reveal, protected persistence, bounded completeness                         |\n| Metadata FP/FN reports                 | C11             | Edit/remove/undo/export without suppression side effects                             |\n| Home/Inbox/source observations/charts  | C12,C18         | Runtime and Gateway data, freshness/partial/unknown/attention                        |\n| Five-product Library/specifications    | C12             | Authoring/import/export; only supported Runtime execution                            |\n| Red Team read-only observations        | C13             | Accepted actual reads; no invented live execution                                    |\n| Model/skill read-only observations     | C13             | Accepted actual reads and partial-source disclosure                                  |\n| API Client documents/projects/imports  | C14             | Fresh-input reconciliation, drafts/conflicts/secrets/Git adoption                    |\n| API Client transport/history/catalogue | C15             | Real HTTP/cookies/downloads, scoped auth, no mutation bypass                         |\n| Gateway workspace/config/admin subset  | C16,C17         | Supported scope/options and reviewed multi-step outcomes                             |\n| Gateway inference/logs/telemetry/cost  | C18             | Streaming, route/model selection, operational budgets/limits                         |\n| Harness native run/stream/lifecycle    | C19             | Real Rust engine/protocol, cleanup and no packaged Node runtime                      |\n| Harness identity/protected history     | C20             | Rust SSO/key lifecycle, scope-safe restore/export/delete                             |\n| Harness typed tools/project permission | C21             | Investigation/proposals and enforced existing sandbox restrictions                   |\n| Workspace MCP                          | C22             | Rust auth/grants, exact call approvals and execution evidence                        |\n| Academy identity/account isolation     | C04             | Device OAuth, scope admission, tenant-independent learner identity                   |\n| Academy learner presentation           | C05             | Shared catalog/lessons/checks/sandbox/UI; feature-local gamification                 |\n| Academy Program/exams/certificates     | C06             | Hosted access/timing/grading/award authority and account workflows                   |\n| Academy encrypted offline work         | C07             | Lease/revision/account-aware reading/drafts; explicit submission                     |\n| Reviewed imports/fresh authentication  | C23             | User work, source preservation, restart/rollback; no old approvals                   |\n| Native UX/privacy/measured performance | C01–C24         | Per-chunk checks plus cumulative actual native quality closure                       |\n| Controlled live behavior               | C25             | Designated scope, real outcomes, readback/cleanup, honest gaps                       |\n| Signed installed package/update        | C26             | DMG/notary/Gatekeeper, exact bytes, fresh user, coexistence/rollback                 |\n\n## Required per-workflow ledger\n\nThe [workflow ledger](../architecture/workflows.md) expands these families into\n66 operation/workflow classes. C01 records machine-readable evidence rows and\nconsuming chunks map exact supported operations/options before implementation.\nEvery row needs an ID, baseline source, current classification, responsible chunk,\nexact SDK/shared dependency contract, and independent expectations. Preserve four\nevidence categories separately: source implementation, fixture/contract results,\nnative/live qualification, and final installed-artifact qualification. Record\ndenied/unsupported/partial results honestly rather than collapsing them to pass.\n\nG01/C01 adds a live_requirement (required/not_required with reason) and separate\nready/blocked-by-access status to every row under [live-checks.md](live-checks.md).\nThe owner approves the expanded list before C25. Missing access cannot shrink\nmandatory scope; a reduction requires a recorded owner decision and new review.\nT23 cross-feature offline acceptance applies to local work and pending operations,\nnot just Academy. C24 closes that cumulative matrix.\n\nV2 source completeness alone does not close a row. Each workflow needs applicable\nsuccess and failure assertions, context/authority coverage, native acceptance and\nrequired live/artifact evidence. C25/C26 review the cumulative ledger against\nthe final frozen input set. A required blocked check blocks stable completion.\n\n## Intentional non-goals and retained classifications\n\n- Financial desktop billing/monetization and media-generation infrastructure are\n  excluded. Remote operational cost/limit administration is retained.\n- Exception Patterns remains explicitly synthetic/inert if shown. FP/FN reports\n  do not suppress scans or modify policy.\n- New Red Team execution and dedicated Model Security execution remain outside\n  parity. Their existence in the new SDK does not authorize adding product scope.\n- Academy admin/assessor operations remain web-only. Learner feedback with an\n  administrative namespace is classified by actual authority, not string matching.\n- No browser app, in-app updater, or additional supported OS/architecture is\n  required for first stable v2.\n- Shared Academy appearance replaces the GPUI presentation implementation. Do\n  not infer a pixel clone or identical internal widget/theme catalogue. Preserve\n  theme preference workflows and specify reviewed mappings for imported settings.\n- The generic SCM workbench catalogue does not prove all 193 requests were live\n  tested. Classify its supported execution/admission separately from dedicated\n  workflows and bind its request metadata to a reviewed source snapshot.\n\nManaged scan/identity HTTP deliberately defaults to Direct rather than v1's\nambient system proxy behavior. On mandatory-proxy networks, onboarding/settings\nshows Direct/System/Explicit policy and requires operator selection; a failed\nfirst request must surface proxy setup rather than an unexplained regression.\nGeneric workbench remains System by default. C02/C15 qualify all modes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat crates/desktop-core/tests/ui_v2_harness/main.rs'","aggregated_output":"//! C32: the Harness's decisions, proposals and confirmations in the core,\n//! on the real pinned engine against the synthetic Gateway that plays the\n//! model (screens/harness.md; provenance P45, P47–P49): desktop reads are\n//! decided in the page, changes need the native confirmation, the key\n//! rotation hand-off and the workspace guardrail are staged for review only,\n//! the MCP catalog is read once allowed, and a confirmation that outlives\n//! its conversation runs nothing.\n\n#[allow(dead_code)]\n#[path = \"../context_credentials/support.rs\"]\nmod support;\n\n#[allow(dead_code, unused_imports)]\n#[path = \"../harness_process/desk.rs\"]\nmod desk;\n\nuse std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\nuse std::sync::Arc;\nuse std::time::Duration;\n\nuse serde_json::{Value, json};\n\nuse crate::desk::*;\n\n/// The Harness desk with the management inventories the proposals review.\nasync fn desk() -> Desk {\n    let desk = desk_with(Some(real_engine()), None).await;\n    desk.gateway.lock().expect(\"gateway\").hook = Some(Arc::new(|seen| {\n        let target = seen.request_line.split(' ').nth(1)?;\n        let path = target.split_once('?').map_or(target, |(p, _)| p);\n        let body = match path {\n            p if p.starts_with(\"/aisec/v1/mgmt/topics/tsg/\") => json!({\"custom_topics\": [\n                {\"topic_id\": \"11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111\", \"topic_name\": \"Finance\",\n                 \"revision\": 1, \"description\": \"Money talk\"}]}),\n            p if p.starts_with(\"/aisec/v1/mgmt/apikeys/tsg/\") => json!({\"api_keys\": [\n                {\"api_key_id\": \"key-1\", \"api_key_name\": \"Runtime\", \"api_key_last8\": \"abcd1234\",\n                 \"cust_app\": \"Support bot\", \"expiration\": \"2027-01-01T00:00:00Z\", \"revoked\": false,\n                 \"status\": \"ACTIVE\"}]}),\n            _ => return None,\n        };\n        Some(json_reply(200, &body))\n    }));\n    desk\n}\n\nfn tool(desk: &Desk, namespace: Option<&str>, name: &str, arguments: Value) {\n    desk.gateway.lock().expect(\"gateway\").answer = Answer::Tool {\n        namespace: namespace.map(str::to_owned),\n        name: name.to_owned(),\n        arguments: arguments.to_string(),\n    };\n}\n\n/// The bodies of the Gateway requests that carried a tool's output.\nfn outputs(desk: &Desk) -> Vec<String> {\n    desk.requests(&format!(\"{RUNTIME}/responses\"))\n        .into_iter()\n        .filter_map(|s| {\n            let body: Value = serde_json::from_slice(&s.body).ok()?;\n            let last = body[\"input\"].as_array()?.last()?.clone();\n            (last[\"type\"] == \"function_call_output\").then(|| last[\"output\"].to_string())\n        })\n        .collect()\n}\n\nfn management_reads(desk: &Desk) -> usize {\n    desk.requests(\"/aisec/v1/mgmt/\").len()\n}\n\n/// A disposable project folder in the build's own scratch space.\nfn project() -> PathBuf {\n    let dir = Path::new(env!(\"CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR\"))\n        .canonicalize()\n        .expect(\"fixture\")\n        .join(format!(\"airs-c21-project-{}\", hex::encode(rand_bytes())));\n    std::fs::create_dir_all(&dir).expect(\"fixture\");\n    for n in 0..3 {\n        std::fs::write(dir.join(format!(\"file-{n}.txt\")), format!(\"content {n}\\n\"))\n            .expect(\"fixture\");\n    }\n    dir\n}\n\nasync fn choose_project(desk: &mut Desk, dir: &Path) {\n    desk.adapters.folders.reply(Some(dir.to_path_buf()));\n    let context = desk.context();\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"chooseHarnessProject\", \"context\": context}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"choose\");\n    let want = dir.to_str().expect(\"utf8\").to_owned();\n    assert!(\n        settle(|| desk.json()[\"harness\"][\"project\"][\"path\"] == want.as_str()).await,\n        \"{}\",\n        desk.json()[\"harness\"][\"project\"]\n    );\n}\n\nasync fn ready(desk: &mut Desk) -> String {\n    desk.ready(None).await\n}\n\nasync fn answered_with(desk: &mut Desk, predicate: impl Fn(&Value) -> bool) -> Value {\n    // A desktop read waits for the operator's decision in the page (C32):\n    // these tests allow each one as it is asked.\n    let deadline = std::time::Instant::now() + Duration::from_secs(40);\n    loop {\n        let c = desk.conversation();\n        if predicate(&c) {\n            break;\n        }\n        assert!(std::time::Instant::now() < deadline, \"{c}\");\n        let reads: Vec<Value> = c[\"approvals\"]\n            .as_array()\n            .map(|a| {\n                a.iter()\n                    .filter(|a| a[\"kind\"] == \"desktopRead\")\n                    .cloned()\n                    .collect()\n            })\n            .unwrap_or_default();\n        for read in reads {\n            let _ = desk\n                .send(\n                    json!({\"kind\": \"decideHarnessApproval\", \"conversation\": c[\"id\"],\n                    \"approval\": read[\"id\"], \"allow\": true}),\n                )\n                .await;\n        }\n        tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(50)).await;\n    }\n    desk.conversation()\n}\n\nfn entry<'a>(c: &'a Value, role: &str) -> Option<&'a Value> {\n    c[\"entries\"]\n        .as_array()?\n        .iter()\n        .rev()\n        .find(|e| e[\"role\"] == role)\n}\n\n/// C32: the keys lifecycle hands off a rotation as an API key version and\n/// the mcp lifecycle proposes a guardrail of the conversation's own\n/// workspace. Each is staged, never applied (nothing is written), and opens\n/// as the operator's review; the guardrail's review is bound to that\n/// workspace's reference.\n#[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\", worker_threads = 4)]\nasync fn a_rotation_hand_off_and_a_workspace_guardrail_are_staged_never_applied() {\n    let mut desk = desk().await;\n    let id = ready(&mut desk).await;\n    let reference = desk.json()[\"gateway\"][\"selected\"][\"reference\"]\n        .as_str()\n        .expect(\"ref\")\n        .to_owned();\n    tool(\n        &desk,\n        Some(\"airs_desktop\"),\n        \"proposeChange\",\n        json!({\"kind\": \"apiKeys\", \"action\": \"version\", \"target\": \"key-1\",\n            \"body\": {\"cust_app\": \"Support bot\", \"cust_env\": \"production\", \"cust_cloud_provider\": \"aws\",\n                     \"api_key_name\": \"Runtime 2\", \"dp_name\": \"dp-0\", \"revoked\": false,\n                     \"rotation_time_interval\": 30, \"rotation_time_unit\": \"days\"},\n            \"summary\": \"Rotation is a write: start it in Administration\"}),\n    );\n    desk.say(&id, \"Rotate the Support bot key.\")\n        .await\n        .expect(\"sent\");\n    let c = answered_with(&mut desk, |c| c[\"lastTurn\"] == \"completed\").await;\n    assert_eq!(c[\"proposals\"][0][\"state\"], \"staged\", \"{c}\");\n    assert_eq!(c[\"proposals\"][0][\"draft\"][\"kind\"], \"apiKeys\");\n    assert_eq!(c[\"proposals\"][0][\"draft\"][\"action\"], \"version\");\n    tool(\n        &desk,\n        Some(\"airs_desktop\"),\n        \"proposeChange\",\n        json!({\"kind\": \"gatewayGuardrails\", \"action\": \"create\",\n            \"body\": {\"name\": \"mcp-allow-list\", \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"pii-check\", \"parameters\": {\"scan_scope\": \"all_messages\"}}],\n                     \"actions\": {\"deny\": true}},\n            \"summary\": \"Deny MCP servers that are not on the allow list\"}),\n    );\n    desk.say(&id, \"Propose a guardrail.\").await.expect(\"sent\");\n    let c = answered_with(&mut desk, |c| {\n        c[\"proposals\"].as_array().map(Vec::len) == Some(2) && c[\"phase\"] == \"ready\"\n    })\n    .await;\n    assert_eq!(c[\"proposals\"][1][\"state\"], \"staged\", \"{c}\");\n    assert_eq!(\n        c[\"proposals\"][1][\"draft\"][\"workspace\"], reference,\n        \"bound to the conversation's own workspace\"\n    );\n    // Nothing was written by the Harness.\n    assert!(\n        desk.requests(\"/aisec/v1/mgmt/apikey\")\n            .iter()\n            .all(|s| s.request_line.starts_with(\"GET\"))\n    );\n    assert!(\n        desk.requests(&format!(\"{DATA}/guardrails\"))\n            .iter()\n            .all(|s| s.request_line.starts_with(\"GET\"))\n    );\n    // Each opens as the operator's review.\n    for proposal in [\"P-1\", \"P-2\"] {\n        let opened = desk\n            .send(\n                json!({\"kind\": \"reviewHarnessProposal\", \"conversation\": id, \"proposal\": proposal}),\n            )\n            .await;\n        assert!(opened.is_ok(), \"{proposal}: {opened:?}\");\n        assert!(settle(|| !desk.json()[\"changes\"][\"review\"].is_null()).await);\n        let review = desk.json()[\"changes\"][\"review\"][\"review\"].clone();\n        desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"discardChange\", \"review\": review}))\n            .await\n            .expect(\"discarded\");\n    }\n    // A Gateway delete or a key rotation in place is never staged.\n    for (kind, action) in [(\"gatewayGuardrails\", \"delete\"), (\"apiKeys\", \"rotate\")] {\n        tool(\n            &desk,\n            Some(\"airs_desktop\"),\n            \"proposeChange\",\n            json!({\"kind\": kind, \"action\": action, \"target\": \"x-1\", \"summary\": \"s\"}),\n        );\n        desk.say(&id, \"Try it.\").await.expect(\"sent\");\n        answered_with(&mut desk, |c| {\n            c[\"phase\"] == \"ready\" && c[\"lastTurn\"].is_string()\n        })\n        .await;\n        let last = outputs(&desk).last().cloned().unwrap_or_default();\n        assert!(\n            last.contains(\"This tool or its arguments are unavailable.\"),\n            \"{last}\"\n        );\n    }\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.conversation()[\"proposals\"].as_array().map(Vec::len),\n        Some(2)\n    );\n    desk.end(&id).await;\n}\n\n/// C32 (R1): a decision is classified by the core. A desktop read is\n/// read-only and decided in the page (declined, nothing is read); a command\n/// with changes allowed may change the project, and in-page consent alone\n/// never runs it: only the native confirmation does.\n#[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\", worker_threads = 4)]\nasync fn reads_are_decided_in_the_page_and_changes_need_the_native_confirmation() {\n    let mut desk = desk().await;\n    let id = ready(&mut desk).await;\n    // A read, declined: nothing is read and the engine is told so.\n    tool(\n        &desk,\n        Some(\"airs_desktop\"),\n        \"inventory\",\n        json!({\"resource\": \"apiKeys\", \"limit\": 5}),\n    );\n    let reads = management_reads(&desk);\n    desk.say(&id, \"Which API keys exist?\").await.expect(\"sent\");\n    assert!(\n        settle_for(40, || desk.conversation()[\"approvals\"]\n            .as_array()\n            .is_some_and(|a| a.len() == 1))\n        .await\n    );\n    let read = desk.conversation()[\"approvals\"][0].clone();\n    assert_eq!(read[\"kind\"], \"desktopRead\");\n    assert_eq!(read[\"effect\"], \"readOnly\");\n    assert_eq!(read[\"server\"], \"airs_desktop\");\n    assert_eq!(read[\"tool\"], \"inventory\");\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"decideHarnessApproval\", \"conversation\": id, \"approval\": read[\"id\"], \"allow\": false}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"declined\");\n    let c = answered_with(&mut desk, |c| {\n        c[\"phase\"] == \"ready\" && c[\"lastTurn\"].is_string()\n    })\n    .await;\n    assert_eq!(management_reads(&desk), reads, \"nothing was read\");\n    assert_eq!(entry(&c, \"tool\").expect(\"entry\")[\"state\"], \"declined\");\n    assert!(\n        outputs(&desk)\n            .last()\n            .is_some_and(|o| o.contains(\"declined this read\"))\n    );\n    desk.end(&id).await;\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"clearHarness\", \"conversation\": id}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"cleared\");\n    // A command with changes allowed: the sheet refused, nothing runs.\n    let dir = project();\n    choose_project(&mut desk, &dir).await;\n    let context = desk.context();\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"setHarnessWrite\", \"context\": context, \"write\": true}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"write\");\n    let reference = desk.json()[\"gateway\"][\"selected\"][\"reference\"]\n        .as_str()\n        .expect(\"ref\")\n        .to_owned();\n    let id = desk.start(&reference).await.expect(\"started\");\n    assert!(settle_for(30, || desk.conversation()[\"phase\"] == \"ready\").await);\n    tool(\n        &desk,\n        None,\n        \"exec_command\",\n        json!({\"cmd\": \"echo c32 > c32.txt\"}),\n    );\n    desk.say(&id, \"Write a file.\").await.expect(\"sent\");\n    assert!(\n        settle_for(40, || desk.conversation()[\"approvals\"]\n            .as_array()\n            .is_some_and(|a| a.len() == 1))\n        .await\n    );\n    let change = desk.conversation()[\"approvals\"][0].clone();\n    assert_eq!(change[\"kind\"], \"command\");\n    assert_eq!(change[\"effect\"], \"mayChange\");\n    desk.adapters.confirmer.auto(Some(false));\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"decideHarnessApproval\", \"conversation\": id, \"approval\": change[\"id\"], \"allow\": true}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"asked natively\");\n    tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(800)).await;\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.conversation()[\"approvals\"][0][\"id\"],\n        change[\"id\"],\n        \"still pending: in-page consent alone does not run it\"\n    );\n    assert!(!dir.join(\"c32.txt\").exists(), \"nothing ran\");\n    // Accepted in the native sheet: it runs once.\n    desk.adapters.confirmer.auto(Some(true));\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"decideHarnessApproval\", \"conversation\": id, \"approval\": change[\"id\"], \"allow\": true}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"asked natively\");\n    answered_with(&mut desk, |c| {\n        c[\"phase\"] == \"ready\"\n            && c[\"approvals\"].as_array().is_some_and(Vec::is_empty)\n            && c[\"lastTurn\"].is_string()\n    })\n    .await;\n    assert!(\n        settle(|| dir.join(\"c32.txt\").exists()).await,\n        \"it ran after the native confirmation\"\n    );\n    desk.end(&id).await;\n}\n\n/// C32 (R7): the mcp lifecycle's read is the desktop's own `mcpServers`\n/// tool: it waits for the operator's decision in the page and, allowed,\n/// reads the conversation workspace's MCP catalog (`GatewayRead::McpServers`)\n/// and gives the engine the servers it lists.\n#[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\", worker_threads = 4)]\nasync fn the_mcp_catalog_is_read_for_the_engine_only_once_the_operator_allows_it() {\n    let mut desk = desk().await;\n    let fast = desk\n        .gateway\n        .lock()\n        .expect(\"gateway\")\n        .hook\n        .clone()\n        .expect(\"hook\");\n    desk.gateway.lock().expect(\"gateway\").hook = Some(Arc::new(move |seen| {\n        let target = seen.request_line.split(' ').nth(1)?;\n        if target.starts_with(&format!(\"{DATA}/mcp-servers\")) {\n            return Some(json_reply(\n                200,\n                &json!({\"object\": \"list\", \"total\": 1, \"data\": [\n                {\"id\": \"mcp-1\", \"name\": \"scratch-tools\", \"slug\": \"scratch-tools\",\n                 \"url\": \"https://mcp.example/scratch-tools/mcp\", \"status\": \"active\",\n                 \"workspace_id\": WS_A, \"last_updated_at\": \"2026-10-28T00:00:00Z\", \"auth_type\": \"oauth\",\n                 \"object\": \"mcp_server\"}]}),\n            ));\n        }\n        fast(seen)\n    }));\n    let id = ready(&mut desk).await;\n    tool(&desk, Some(\"airs_desktop\"), \"mcpServers\", json!({}));\n    desk.say(&id, \"Which MCP servers does this workspace have?\")\n        .await\n        .expect(\"sent\");\n    assert!(\n        settle_for(40, || desk.conversation()[\"approvals\"]\n            .as_array()\n            .is_some_and(|a| a.len() == 1))\n        .await\n    );\n    let read = desk.conversation()[\"approvals\"][0].clone();\n    assert_eq!(\n        (\n            read[\"kind\"].as_str(),\n            read[\"tool\"].as_str(),\n            read[\"effect\"].as_str()\n        ),\n        (Some(\"desktopRead\"), Some(\"mcpServers\"), Some(\"readOnly\"))\n    );\n    assert!(\n        desk.requests(&format!(\"{DATA}/mcp-servers\")).is_empty(),\n        \"nothing read before the decision\"\n    );\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"decideHarnessApproval\", \"conversation\": id, \"approval\": read[\"id\"], \"allow\": true}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"allowed\");\n    let c = answered_with(&mut desk, |c| {\n        c[\"phase\"] == \"ready\" && c[\"lastTurn\"].is_string()\n    })\n    .await;\n    assert_eq!(\n        desk.requests(&format!(\"{DATA}/mcp-servers\")).len(),\n        1,\n        \"read once\"\n    );\n    assert_eq!(entry(&c, \"tool\").expect(\"entry\")[\"state\"], \"complete\");\n    assert!(\n        outputs(&desk)\n            .last()\n            .is_some_and(|o| o.contains(\"scratch-tools\")),\n        \"{:?}\",\n        outputs(&desk)\n    );\n    desk.end(&id).await;\n}\n\n/// C32 (attempt-02 optional): a native confirmation still open when its\n/// conversation ends is dismissed, and an acceptance that arrives late runs\n/// nothing.\n#[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\", worker_threads = 4)]\nasync fn a_confirmation_that_outlives_its_conversation_runs_nothing() {\n    let mut desk = desk().await;\n    let dir = project();\n    choose_project(&mut desk, &dir).await;\n    let context = desk.context();\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"setHarnessWrite\", \"context\": context, \"write\": true}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"write\");\n    let id = ready(&mut desk).await;\n    tool(\n        &desk,\n        None,\n        \"exec_command\",\n        json!({\"cmd\": \"echo late > late.txt\"}),\n    );\n    desk.say(&id, \"Write a file.\").await.expect(\"sent\");\n    assert!(\n        settle_for(40, || desk.conversation()[\"approvals\"]\n            .as_array()\n            .is_some_and(|a| a.len() == 1))\n        .await\n    );\n    let change = desk.conversation()[\"approvals\"][0].clone();\n    assert_eq!(change[\"effect\"], \"mayChange\");\n    // The sheet stays open: the operator has not answered yet.\n    desk.adapters.confirmer.auto(None);\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"decideHarnessApproval\", \"conversation\": id, \"approval\": change[\"id\"], \"allow\": true}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"asked natively\");\n    assert!(\n        settle(|| desk.adapters.confirmer.held() == 1).await,\n        \"the sheet is shown\"\n    );\n    let nonce = desk\n        .adapters\n        .confirmer\n        .requests()\n        .last()\n        .expect(\"a request\")\n        .0;\n    // The conversation ends while the sheet is open: it is dismissed.\n    desk.end(&id).await;\n    assert!(\n        settle(|| desk.adapters.confirmer.dismissed().contains(&nonce)).await,\n        \"dismissed with its conversation\"\n    );\n    // A late acceptance runs nothing.\n    let _ = desk.adapters.confirmer.complete(true);\n    tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(800)).await;\n    assert!(!dir.join(\"late.txt\").exists(), \"nothing ran\");\n}\n\n#[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\", worker_threads = 4)]\nasync fn the_opening_message_is_kept_whole_beside_its_shortened_title() {\n    // A contextual restart prefills the opening question, never the title\n    // (screens/harness.md; attempt-12 R1).\n    let mut desk = desk().await;\n    let id = ready(&mut desk).await;\n    let opening = format!(\n        \"Investigate the Finance topic.\\nList every key that expires before the audit, {}and explain.\",\n        \"with its owner and its application, \".repeat(4)\n    );\n    assert!(opening.chars().count() > 160);\n    desk.say(&id, &opening).await.expect(\"sent\");\n    let c = answered_with(&mut desk, |c| {\n        c[\"phase\"] == \"ready\" && c[\"lastTurn\"] == \"completed\"\n    })\n    .await;\n    assert_eq!(c[\"opening\"], opening.as_str(), \"{c}\");\n    assert!(settle(|| !desk.conversation()[\"savedAt\"].is_null()).await);\n    let history = c[\"historyId\"].as_str().expect(\"id\").to_owned();\n    desk.say(&id, \"And the second question?\")\n        .await\n        .expect(\"sent\");\n    let _ = answered_with(&mut desk, |c| {\n        c[\"phase\"] == \"ready\" && c[\"entries\"].as_array().is_some_and(|e| e.len() >= 4)\n    })\n    .await;\n    desk.end(&id).await;\n    // Ended, it still shows its opening whole.\n    assert_eq!(desk.conversation()[\"opening\"], opening.as_str());\n    // Saved: listed by a shortened one-line title, opened with the opening whole.\n    let context = desk.context();\n    let workspace = desk.json()[\"gateway\"][\"selected\"][\"reference\"].clone();\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"listHarnessHistory\", \"context\": context, \"workspace\": workspace}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"list\");\n    assert!(settle(|| desk.json()[\"harness\"][\"history\"][\"state\"] == \"ready\").await);\n    let listed = desk.json()[\"harness\"][\"history\"][\"conversations\"].clone();\n    let title = listed\n        .as_array()\n        .and_then(|l| l.iter().find(|c| c[\"id\"] == history.as_str()))\n        .and_then(|c| c[\"title\"].as_str())\n        .expect(\"listed\")\n        .to_owned();\n    assert!(title.ends_with('…') && !title.contains('\\n'), \"{title}\");\n    desk.send(\n        json!({\"kind\": \"openHarnessHistory\", \"context\": context, \"workspace\": workspace, \"id\": history}),\n    )\n    .await\n    .expect(\"open\");\n    assert!(settle(|| desk.json()[\"harness\"][\"history\"][\"opened\"][\"id\"] == history.as_str()).await);\n    let opened = desk.json()[\"harness\"][\"history\"][\"opened\"].clone();\n    assert_eq!(opened[\"opening\"], opening.as_str(), \"{opened}\");\n    assert_eq!(opened[\"title\"], title.as_str());\n    let first = desk.json()[\"harness\"][\"history\"][\"lastOpen\"].clone();\n    assert_eq!(first[\"id\"], history.as_str(), \"{first}\");\n    assert!(first[\"failure\"].is_null());\n    // A record that cannot be read: each open settles with its own receipt,\n    // also when it fails as the one before it did (attempt-13 R1).\n    let missing = \"00000000-0000-8000-8000-000000000000\";\n    let mut sequence = first[\"sequence\"].as_u64().expect(\"sequence\");\n    for _ in 0..2 {\n        desk.send(\n            json!({\"kind\": \"openHarnessHistory\", \"context\": context, \"workspace\": workspace, \"id\": missing}),\n        )\n        .await\n        .expect(\"open\");\n        assert!(\n            settle(|| {\n                let l = &desk.json()[\"harness\"][\"history\"][\"lastOpen\"];\n                l[\"id\"] == missing && l[\"sequence\"].as_u64() > Some(sequence)\n            })\n            .await\n        );\n        let h = desk.json()[\"harness\"][\"history\"].clone();\n        assert_eq!(h[\"lastOpen\"][\"failure\"], \"missing\", \"{h}\");\n        assert_eq!(h[\"problem\"], \"missing\");\n        assert_eq!(h[\"busy\"], false);\n        sequence = h[\"lastOpen\"][\"sequence\"].as_u64().expect(\"sequence\");\n    }\n}\n\n#[tokio::test(flavor = \"multi_thread\", worker_threads = 4)]\nasync fn a_named_send_is_taken_once_and_reported_with_the_message_it_became() {\n    // A send whose receipt was lost is settled by the core's word (attempt-16 R1).\n    let mut desk = desk().await;\n    let id = ready(&mut desk).await;\n    let submission = \"0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef\";\n    let send = json!({\"kind\": \"sendHarness\", \"conversation\": id, \"prompt\": \"Same words\", \"submission\": submission});\n    desk.send(send.clone()).await.expect(\"sent\");\n    // The same delivery again (its receipt was lost): taken once, nothing sent again.\n    desk.send(send).await.expect(\"taken already\");\n    let c = answered_with(&mut desk, |c| {\n        c[\"phase\"] == \"ready\" && c[\"lastTurn\"] == \"completed\"\n    })\n    .await;\n    assert_eq!(\n        c[\"submissions\"],\n        json!([{\"submission\": submission, \"entry\": \"u-1\", \"state\": \"delivered\"}]),\n        \"{c}\"\n    );\n    let operators = c[\"entries\"]\n        .as_array()\n        .expect(\"entries\")\n        .iter()\n        .filter(|e| e[\"role\"] == \"operator\")\n        .count();\n    assert_eq!(operators, 1, \"{c}\");\n    // Identical words under another ID are another send, reported as its own.\n    let other = \"fedcba9876543210fedcba9876543210\";\n    desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"sendHarness\", \"conversation\": id, \"prompt\": \"Same words\", \"submission\": other}))\n        .await\n        .expect(\"sent\");\n    let c = answered_with(&mut desk, |c| {\n        c[\"phase\"] == \"ready\" && c[\"submissions\"].as_array().is_some_and(|s| s.len() == 2)\n    })\n    .await;\n    assert_eq!(\n        c[\"submissions\"][1],\n        json!({\"submission\": other, \"entry\": \"u-2\", \"state\": \"delivered\"})\n    );\n    // An ID not of the presentation's form is refused.\n    assert!(\n        desk.send(json!({\"kind\": \"sendHarness\", \"conversation\": id, \"prompt\": \"x\", \"submission\": \"not-hex\"}))\n            .await\n            .is_err()\n    );\n    desk.end(&id).await;\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^(describe|it|test)|''^[ ]+(it|test)'\"\\\\(' apps/desktop/src/v2/harness/harness.test.tsx\n rg -n 'harness|Harness' apps/desktop/src/v2/v2-shell.tsx apps/desktop/src/v2/store.ts\n wc -l crates/desktop-core/src/authority/harness* crates/desktop-core/src/harness* apps/desktop/src/v2/harness/harness.test.tsx\n python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"docs/planning/reviews/C32/attempt-21/source-inventory.json\\\"; i=json.load(open(p)); [print(k,str(v)[:500]) for k,v in i.items() if k\"'!=\"files\"]'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^(describe|it|test)|''^[ ]+(it|test)'\"\\\\(' apps/desktop/src/v2/harness/harness.test.tsx\n rg -n 'harness|Harness' apps/desktop/src/v2/v2-shell.tsx apps/desktop/src/v2/store.ts\n wc -l crates/desktop-core/src/authority/harness* crates/desktop-core/src/harness* apps/desktop/src/v2/harness/harness.test.tsx\n python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"docs/planning/reviews/C32/attempt-21/source-inventory.json\\\"; i=json.load(open(p)); [print(k,str(v)[:500]) for k,v in i.items() if k\"'!=\"files\"]'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"142:describe('v2 Harness', () => {\n143:    it('ships lifecycle fixtures the core contract accepts at every step', () => {\n154:        it(`${l.lifecycle}: the read-only call is approved in the page, its follow-up opens only a review, and ending seals the conversation (V2-T17)`, async () => {\n190:        it(`${l.lifecycle}: declining records the decision and the assistant's declined text, with no follow-up (V2-T17)`, async () => {\n203:    it('keys: the Harness refuses to rotate and hands off; the follow-up follows the rotation stage and never dispatches a mutation (V2-T18)', async () => {\n231:    it('a fresh tenant shows no seeded conversation; its first send starts a user conversation and sends the message once it is ready (V2-T13, I12)', async () => {\n256:    it('sending after a conversation ended clears it and starts a new one', async () => {\n267:    it('contextual navigation into an ended conversation shows the hint; it opens the saved transcript or prefills a new investigation, and clears on navigation', async () => {\n298:    it('a contextual restart of the ended conversation prefills its whole opening question, never its shortened title; a draft is kept and nothing is sent (attempt-12 R1)', async () => {\n319:    it('a contextual restart of an archived conversation reads its record for the whole opening question; a draft is kept and nothing is sent (attempt-12 R1)', async () => {\n344:    it('says when the opening question is not known, or its record could not be read, and never substitutes the title (attempt-12 R1)', async () => {\n384:    it('a repeated read failure of an archived record settles each read by its receipt: loading ends, the failure is said, retry works, the draft stays and nothing starts (attempt-13 R1)', async () => {\n412:    it('a contextual arrival waits for the saved conversations to be listed: the hint appears once its record is, the draft stays and nothing starts (attempt-14 R1)', async () => {\n441:    it('a pending contextual arrival is cancelled by navigation or another workspace, and says when its record is not listed or cannot be (attempt-14 R1)', async () => {\n491:    it('choosing New investigation while an archived record is read retires the contextual restart: its late success or failure changes neither the draft nor the choice (attempt-15 R1)', async () => {\n522:    it('a read refused after the operator chose another investigation says nothing over it (attempt-16 S1)', async () => {\n557:    it('keeps the prerequisites checklist until every one is satisfied', async () => {\n567:    it('keeps the C19–C22 controls: the project, sign-in and MCP panels, saved-conversation management, and the write confirmation after a renewal', async () => {\n586:    it('says when a decision may change things: approving asks for the system confirmation, never in-page consent alone (R1)', async () => {\n608:    it('keeps the first message until a conversation takes it: refused, failed startup and a replacement never lose it or send it elsewhere (R2)', async () => {\n645:    it('a new investigation while one runs ends it and sends to a different conversation; the contextual restart shows its opening question (R3)', async () => {\n674:    it('a pending decision holds a new investigation back', async () => {\n681:    it('a pending decision holds a contextual restart back without losing its hint; an unconfirmed read is never called a failure', async () => {\n707:    it('returns an unsent message to the box with the sign-in failure, and resends nothing (R4)', async () => {\n718:    it('shows how the conversation stands: a failed start, a cut or failed answer, a failed cleanup and an unsaved transcript are never presented as complete or saved (R5)', async () => {\n742:    it('keeps each draft in its tenant, workspace and conversation across navigation and a tenant round trip, sending nothing by itself (R6)', async () => {\n759:    it('keeps the box and the new-investigation choice by workspace ID across navigation and an A/B/A that retires the conversation (attempt-02/03 R1)', async () => {\n781:    it('retires a first send whose conversation ends before it is ready, or whose start is unconfirmed: text kept, controls usable, nothing sent (attempt-02 R2)', async () => {\n806:    it('clears only the submitted text: an edit made while the first send waits, or while a message is delivered, stays (attempt-02 R3)', async () => {\n834:    it('keeps both a returned message and the draft typed meanwhile: the message goes under Not sent with a way back into the box (attempt-02/03 R4)', async () => {\n851:    it('keeps every edit across the starting snapshot: edits before and after it stay in the one box (attempt-03 R2)', async () => {\n868:    it('says truthfully where an unsent first message is: still in the box, or kept under Not sent when the box changed (attempt-03 R3)', async () => {\n897:    it('one Send starts at most one conversation and delivers once, even when the clear publishes before its receipt (attempt-03 R4)', async () => {\n925:    it('keeps a refused or undelivered follow-up beside the edit made while it was delivered, and resends nothing (attempt-04 R1)', async () => {\n959:    it('never calls an unconfirmed send \"not sent\": only the core\\'s word that it took that send settles it, never matching text, and nothing is resent (attempt-04 R2, attempt-16 R1)', async () => {\n981:    it('identical unconfirmed sends in two conversations are settled each by its own conversation only (attempt-06 R1)', async () => {\n1005:    it('two identical unconfirmed sends are settled each by its own ID, once, across renders and a remount (attempt-07 R1, attempt-10 R1)', async () => {\n1029:    it('an admitted retry never settles the unconfirmed original: only the original\\'s own ID does (attempt-08 R1, attempt-09 R1)', async () => {\n1053:    it('an admitted send\\'s delayed entry never settles a later identical unconfirmed send; that send\\'s own ID settles it once (attempt-16 R1)', async () => {\n1090:    it('a send whose receipt was lost and that the core then gave back is never taken as delivered: its exact text stays in the box or under Not sent (attempt-17 R1)', async () => {\n1156:    it('a receipt that arrives after the core gave its send back never clears the returned text, on either send path (attempt-18 R1)', async () => {\n1246:    it('a pending report is never final: a send later given back keeps its exact text beside newer edits, on both send paths and through an A/B/A that retires its conversation (attempt-19 R1)', async () => {\n1309:    it('the rail keeps the conversation\\'s title from its opening after the transcript dropped it, also once ended (attempt-18 R2)', async () => {\n1328:    it('settles an unconfirmed send by the core\\'s word even when the transcript is at its bounds and dropped its oldest entries (attempt-11 R1)', async () => {\n1351:    it('a lost start receipt is never \"no conversation started\": the message stays, sent nowhere (attempt-04 R2, lost start receipt)', async () => {\n1370:    it('settles an unconfirmed send only by a message its own conversation added after it: a repeated prompt or another conversation settles nothing (attempt-05 R1)', async () => {\n1397:    it('a retry whose receipt is lost moves a refused message from Not sent to Not confirmed, truthfully (attempt-05 R2)', async () => {\n1433:    it('a later refused retry never downgrades an earlier unconfirmed send (attempt-06 R1)', async () => {\n1465:    it('confirms an ended conversation with a toast bound to its tenant and context (I10)', async () => {\n1478:    it('a retry whose entry arrives before its receipt never settles the unconfirmed original either (attempt-09 R1)', async () => {\n1517:    it('draws the board: the title band with End conversation, the 244px rail of saved conversations, the transcript with its composer, and the Decisions aside holding the decision (C38)', async () => {\n1550:    it('tells the aside what it cannot decide yet, and names the workspace MCP servers with their standing (C38)', async () => {\n1591:    it('says what the MCP summary knows: not read, reading, failed, partial; every server that is on is listed and the rest are counted (attempt-01 R1)', async () => {\n1612:    it('chooses a folder, names a refused one, allows changes in it and removes it, through the v2 project panel (C21, attempt-01 E2)', async () => {\n1638:    it('keeps a lost receipt as Not confirmed in the v2 panels, naming the action; the next snapshot settles what happened and the page resends nothing (attempt-02 R1)', async () => {\n1713:    it('sets up company sign-in, signs in through the browser, chooses the credential and signs out, through the v2 sign-in panel; a refused save is named (C20, attempt-01 E2)', async () => {\n1762:    it('reads the MCP catalog, turns servers on, signs in and out, says why a server cannot be used and keeps at most eight on, through the v2 MCP panel (C22, attempt-01 E2)', async () => {\n1844:    it('lists, opens, continues, exports and deletes saved conversations, says why one cannot be continued, names unreadable ones and a locked store, through the v2 history panel (C20, attempt-01 E2)', async () => {\napps/desktop/src/v2/v2-shell.tsx:7:import { harnessCredential } from './harness/credential'\napps/desktop/src/v2/v2-shell.tsx:8:import { 