{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/planning/test-catalogue.md\n cat docs/planning/dependencies.md | tail -25\n cat docs/planning/status.md | head -70'","aggregated_output":"# Behavioral and native test catalogue\n\nThese are required future tests and observable assertions, not results already\nexecuted. G01/C01 bind them to exact commands. Each chunk names its applicable\nIDs and adds feature-specific cases. Use fake transports/clocks/stores at real\nmodule interfaces plus literal external fixtures; native and live tests provide\nseparate evidence. Do not assert implementation-private structure for its own sake.\n\n## Core authority and SDK\n\n- **T01 Context isolation:** tenant/workspace/credential switch during a request\n  rejects old replies, retires pending reviews/one-time secrets, and cancels work.\n  Switching back cannot revive authority. Credential replacement and sign-out\n  behave the same way; duplicate completions settle at most once.\n- **T02 Review authority:** forged/stale/replayed/consumed review IDs, changed\n  draft/resource/context, model text, and imported history cannot Apply. Valid\n  operator Apply transmits the exact reviewed operation once.\n- **T03 Unknown outcomes:** disconnect before send, after send, timeout, cancel,\n  401/403/429/5xx, and partial multistep provisioning yield correct states. No\n  automatic mutation/scan replay; offer readback/review/explicit retry where valid.\n- **T04 SDK external contract:** independently authored request/response fixtures\n  verify method/path/body/headers/options, pagination/multipart limits, unknown\n  enum/action preservation, sanitized errors, and no dropped options.\n- **T05 Credential confinement:** scan-only setup works; management/inference/MCP\n  credentials are separate. Deny wrong-origin redirects or custom endpoint\n  changes that would forward a credential without an explicitly reviewed new\n  destination binding. Preserve legitimate operator-reviewed endpoint overrides\n  and explicitly selected nonsecret tenant-profile import; whitelist metadata,\n  discard embedded secrets and never follow credential-file references.\n  No implicit environment/tenant file\n  loading, upstream fallback, persistent renderer storage, or secret log fields.\n- **T06 Protected storage:** locked/denied/unavailable/corrupt store, interrupted\n  write/reset, session-only mode, restart, explicit one-time reveal/clipboard,\n  and cleanup. No plaintext fallback; v1 namespaces remain untouched.\n- **T07 Lifecycle:** bounded concurrent work, cancellation, queue backpressure,\n  superseding reads, app close/restart, sleep/wake, expired credentials, and\n  monotonic versus wall-clock decisions. UI remains responsive during work.\n\n## Presentation and Academy\n\n- **T08 Shared presentation:** web and desktop consumers build from the same\n  reviewed shared source; themes/fonts/routes render correctly. General desktop\n  screens mount no Academy gamification/account effects or web manager routes.\n- **T09 Native UI:** actual Tauri command path, menus/shortcuts, keyboard-only\n  workflow, focus restoration, VoiceOver labels/order, zoom/large text, themes,\n  reduced motion, long/empty/error content, and window resizing. Mock IPC tests\n  alone cannot establish these. macOS WebDriver availability must be verified;\n  use supported native accessibility/automation or recorded manual steps.\n- **T10 Academy identity:** device grant, pending/slow_down/expiry/cancel, refresh,\n  revocation, wrong issuer/client/scope, account switch/sign-out, and stale replies.\n  Token management stays Rust-owned. The learner account is independent of tenant.\n- **T11 Learning authority:** client bundles contain no answer keys/private lab\n  evaluation, privileged routes, or assessor tokens. Forged verdict/award/local\n  exam clock cannot pass; the hosted backend decides access, grading, and awards.\n  Signed-in denial differs from guest sign-in; sandbox never uses tenant secrets.\n- **T12 Offline work:** download lease/revision/account access, encrypted draft\n  save/restart, locked vault, sign-out/account switch, withdrawn content, duplicate\n  submission IDs, changed draft versions, and reconnection. No deferred action\n  replay. Valid local work remains usable without claiming offline grading.\n\n## Workflows and Harness\n\n- **T13 Collection semantics:** exact capability subsets, large collections,\n  bounded pagination/truncation, search/filter/page resets, stale/partial cache,\n  consistent Home/Inbox source facts, and no false complete/zero/absent claims.\n- **T14 API Client documents:** edit/save/conflict while typing, invalid input,\n  environment/secret separation, import/path traversal/size errors, multipart,\n  cookies/redirect auth, cancellation, history/download, Git/profile adoption,\n  and recovery from interrupted writes. Arbitrary workbench targets cannot borrow\n  privileged application credentials through renderer-supplied references.\n- **T15 Harness process:** actual native binary and bounded bootstrap/JSONL\n  protocol, malformed/oversized frames, correlation/duplicates, queue pressure,\n  crash/EOF/cancel, context change, graceful/forced cleanup, and missing/tampered\n  resources. No PATH launcher fallback or plaintext rollout/history.\n- **T16 Harness authority:** typed investigation/proposal tools, active-draft\n  protection, no engine Apply, one-time secrets absent from model context,\n  read-only project defaults, approved single-process command restrictions,\n  forbidden descendants/pipelines, stale decisions, and history replay.\n- **T17 Inference/MCP identity:** pinned Gateway origin; SSO PKCE/state/nonce/\n  issuer/client/audience/time/signature/JWKS/algorithm/key-rotation validation;\n  sleep/refresh/revoke/identity changes;\n  distinct inference/MCP grants; fixed conversation server scope; exact call-item\n  approvals; changed revision/grant; denied tools; trace/execution evidence.\n  No direct upstream provider fallback or global cross-workspace MCP authority.\n\n## Import, quality, and artifacts\n\n- **T18 Import transaction:** dry-run selection, versions/source lock, account\n  match, protected source reads, malformed/oversized/traversal inputs, interruption\n  at each commit point, restart, duplicate import, destination conflict, rollback,\n  and source-byte preservation. No credentials/sessions/approvals transfer.\n- **T19 Diagnostics privacy:** seeded canary secrets and customer content absent\n  from logs/crash files/exports by default; explicit redacted export; correct\n  retention/reset; no analytics/crash upload attempts; encrypted user history\n  remains a distinct intentional storage feature.\n- **T20 Performance:** named macOS hardware/OS/workloads, cold/warm startup, idle\n  and scan/large-list/streaming/Harness memory, main-thread responsiveness, file\n  and DMG footprint. Record methodology, repetitions, distribution and baseline;\n  set core budgets in C03 and register later workload budgets at the introducing\n  chunk's entry before implementation/acceptance measurement. See the budget\n  governance below; C24/C26 compare with pre-registered values.\n- **T21 Controlled live:** designated account/tenant/entitlements and disposable\n  resources, explicit operation allowlist/budgets, sanitized request IDs, readback,\n  cleanup receipts, deny/error cases, and unresolved outcome handling. Missing\n  access or unsupported operations remain blocked; no destructive production tests.\n- **T22 Installed package:** signed/notarized/stapled DMG, Gatekeeper/quarantine,\n  mount/drag/install/launch/relaunch with fresh user/home and no developer checkout,\n  PATH Node/Bun/managed CLI disabled, actual Rust sidecar, runtime inventory/hash\n  integrity, no hidden backend download, safe uninstall/reset/coexistence,\n  manual update, previous-version rollback, and preserved user work.\n- **T23 Cross-feature offline:** launch offline and read/edit each applicable\n  local category: saved cases, FP/FN reports, API Client documents, protected\n  Harness history, configuration drafts, and Academy work. Mark remote data as\n  stale/unknown as appropriate. Offline drafts do not retain valid Apply authority;\n  reconnect requires fresh readback/review when needed. Pending reviews, scans,\n  inference turns, generic HTTP mutations and MCP/tool calls never resubmit on\n  reconnect. Offer explicit retry while preserving uncertain remote outcomes.\n  Bind to C03,C09–C12,C14–C15,C17–C18,C20–C22 and cumulative C24.\n\n## Performance budget governance\n\nC03 registers numeric budgets and named methods for the shell/scan workloads\nbefore C04. Also register the later workload catalogue and owning chunks.\nBefore implementing/measuring a newly introduced workload, its owning chunk\ncommits a numeric budget, hardware/OS, dataset, measurement method and rationale:\nC11/C13 large collections; C15 large HTTP bodies/downloads; C18 streaming/charts;\nC19 native-engine startup/memory; C20 history; C21/C22 tool/MCP workloads.\nDo not wait until C24 to fit limits to observed results.\n\nA budget change requires a versioned rationale, original failures/results, and\nowner or independent reviewer acknowledgement recorded in the receipt. It cannot\nsilently erase a regression. Benchmark evidence records the pre-registered budget\nhash; the controller rejects retroactive or mismatched budget inputs. C24/C26\ncompare against those exact pre-committed values, including changed-budget history.\n\nNormal bounded metadata reads or credential refresh prerequisites for an explicit\noperation are not deferred business-action replay. Tests must distinguish these\nfrom silently resubmitting scans, writes, grading, or tool calls after reconnect.\n\nBefore review, challenge security-critical tests with a relevant deliberate\nbehavior mutation or equivalent negative probe. Show that violating an invariant\nfails the test; do not create an exhaustive mutation framework or mirror every\nimplementation detail. Run mutations only in isolated disposable copies.\n  reversible resources, budgets, and cleanup/readback before C25 execution.\n  Prod configuration discovery is not mutation authorization. Missing access is\n  a real dependency gap; never report skipped tests as passed.\n- **Hosted OAuth registrations:** G01 maps reuse/new-client/redirect/scope needs\n  for Academy device authorization, Harness company SSO and MCP. Responsible\n  Academy/Gateway/IdP operators own authorized staging/configuration changes and\n  deployment. V2 identity alone neither proves a new registration is required\n  nor authorizes production changes. Resolve before the consuming live tests.\n- **Signing:** identify an authorized Developer ID, provisioning/entitlement\n  requirements, notarization access, and a native acceptance host. Access secrets\n  only at use time through approved storage, never committed plan variables.\n\n## Official host references\n\nTauri supports Rust commands and async messages between presentation and host;\nthe selected command/module interface still requires G01 design and review.\n[Calling Rust](https://v2.tauri.app/develop/calling-rust/)\n\nWindow/WebView capability grants require deliberate scoping; renderer grants do\nnot replace Rust's application authority checks.\n[Capabilities](https://v2.tauri.app/security/capabilities/)\n\nDMG distribution and macOS signing are separate from successful compilation.\n[DMG packaging](https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/dmg/),\n[macOS signing/notarization](https://v2.tauri.app/distribute/sign/macos/).\n# Current state\n\nG00 and G01 passed (historical Claude reviews). C01–C04 and the P01 cumulative review completed on\n2026-10-17; C05–C07 and the P02 cumulative review completed on 2026-10-18;\nC08–C12 and the P03 cumulative review completed on 2026-10-19; C13–C15 and\nthe P04 cumulative review completed on 2026-10-20; C16–C18 and the P05\ncumulative review completed on 2026-10-21; C19–C22 and the P06 cumulative\nreview completed on 2026-10-23; C23–C24 and the P07 cumulative review\ncompleted on 2026-10-24. P08/C26 remains open; the owner-authorized P09\nintegration is now at fresh Worf cumulative native qualification after C44 full-9 closure.\nWorf native generation 01 passed all 19 mapped drivers with C44 last, including\nC43's 24 behaviors and 48 rows. It is preserved complete with the exact executable\nunder `evidence/P09/native-history/Worf-generation-01-complete-20261101`.\nFresh check attempt-03 passed 17/18 checks but failed import test relaunch/timing\nassertions on all three fixture runs. The corrected harness uses the production\nshutdown hook, a durable receipt boundary and a read-only fixture observer of the\narmed cut; the full import suite now passes 23/23 with every assertion retained.\nNative generation 02 is rebuilt with an exact before/after input seal; C36 passed,\nand all remaining mapped drivers will repeat before\nfresh checks and C29–C32/P09 reviews. C24-N06 and C31-N01/N04 remain superseded raw\nfailures under the unchanged map. No current native or review pass is transferred\nto changed inputs.\nUse [WORF-START-HERE](WORF-START-HERE.md) for the 2026-11-01 checkpoint and next commands. D026 (2026-10-17) makes Codex the independent reviewer of every chunk\nand of a cumulative review after every phase, each requiring at least 9 in all\nfive dimensions with empty required fixes, blockers and evidence gaps. D034 (2026-10-18, owner rule) lets a chunk complete at 8/10 with no\nblockers; each phase review still needs 9/10, after every chunk accepted below\n9 is raised to a passing review.\n\n| Gate/chunk | State | Evidence/next action |\n|---|---|---|\n| G00 | Passed (historical) | Attempt03 scored 9 in all five dimensions |\n| G01 | Passed (historical) | Attempt05 scored 9 in all five dimensions; fingerprint covers commit 931916b inputs only |\n| C01 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-04 scored 9 in all five dimensions; bootstrap agreement passed (52 adversarial cases including 16 typed, 2 controls); committed as ce5bd8d and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempts 01–03 failed and were remediated (records retained) |\n| C02 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-03 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as dfcf9bb and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempts 01–02 failed and were remediated (records retained) |\n| C03 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-02 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 1b69852 and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempt-01 (9/8/8/8/8) remediated (`reviews/C03/remediation-attempt-01.md`); budgets v3 acknowledged; C24 owns the typed-input memory observation |\n| P01 | **Complete**: Codex phase attempt-02 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 80d6c51 and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempt-01 (9/8/9/8/8) remediated (`reviews/P01/remediation-attempt-01.md`); 38/38 integrated native checks; budgets re-measured on the P01 bundle |\n| C04 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-03 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 4c13792 and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempts 01 (8/7/7/8/7) and 02 (9/8/9/8/8) remediated (`reviews/C04/remediation-attempt-0{1,2}.md`); D028 recorded |\n| C05 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-03 passed; committed as 7afdd9b and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempts 01–02 remediated (`reviews/C05/remediation-attempt-0{1,2}.md`) |\n| C06 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-05 passed; committed as 8718ac9 and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempts 01–04 remediated (records retained); D030 recorded |\n| C07 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-06 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 960e340 and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempts 01–05 remediated (`reviews/C07/remediation-attempt-0{1..5}.md`); D031 and D032 recorded |\n| P02 | **Complete**: Codex phase attempt-01 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 3decccc and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Integrated native checks for C04–C07 and the workload budget on the P02 bundle |\n| C08 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034 (c07cc8b), then raised; Codex attempt-03 passed with 9 in all five dimensions; committed as ada9234 and verified | Follow-ups R1–R3/E1 remediated (`reviews/C08/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C09 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034 (aef8431), then raised; Codex attempt-03 passed with 9 in all five dimensions; committed as deb34c6 and verified | Follow-ups remediated, including native sheet retirement and reveal ownership (`reviews/C09/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C10 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034 (90dbc40), then raised; Codex attempt-03 passed with 9 in all five dimensions; committed as a38b4f8 and verified | Follow-ups remediated, including production NSOpenPanel evidence (`reviews/C10/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C11 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034 (0e4bda6), then raised; Codex attempt-03 passed with 9 in all five dimensions; committed as aec2cbc and verified | Follow-ups remediated, including production save panel evidence (`reviews/C11/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C12 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034 (1911da6), then raised; Codex attempt-04 passed with 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 962747b and verified | Attempts 02–03 remediated: status stamps for library outcomes, hardened mutation harness, C12-N11 offline Library (`reviews/C12/follow-ups.md`) |\n| P03 | **Complete**: Codex phase attempt-02 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as bbbad43 and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempt-01 R1 (context-bound Playground handoff) remediated (`reviews/P03/follow-ups.md`); integrated native checks for C08–C12, the C11 workload and 129/129 mutation probes on the P03 bundle |\n| C13 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034 (0d105e0), then raised; Codex attempt-03 passed with 9 in all five dimensions; committed as bdd57c2 and verified | Follow-ups R1–R4/E1 remediated, including nested rated targets, pagination shape and capped totals (`reviews/C13/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C14 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034 (8d219b0), then raised; Codex attempt-06 passed with 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 0c6a604 and verified | Follow-ups R1/R5/R6 remediated: body ownership by the file reached and by schema role, unchanged saves superseding drafts, bounded discovery (`reviews/C14/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C15 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034 (6d78143), then raised; Codex attempt-04 passed with 9 in all five dimensions; committed as e9df1db and verified | Follow-ups R2/R5 remediated: the effective credential set (including the jar Cookie) at registered origins and reviews bound to the credentials sent (`reviews/C15/follow-ups.md`) |\n| P04 | **Complete**: Codex phase attempt-03 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 8d5d436 and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Integrated native checks for C13–C15, the C13 and C15 workloads and 149/149 mutation probes on the P04 bundle |\n| C16 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034 (21266fe), then raised; Codex attempt-03 passed with 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 1811d43 and verified | Follow-ups R1/R2 remediated: models bound to the integration shown and the chosen workspace's detail readable, with C16-N10/N11 (`reviews/C16/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C17 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-03 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 250a8ce and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempts 01–02 remediated (`reviews/C17/remediation-attempt-0{1,2}.md`); D043 recorded |\n| C18 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-04 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 9b5f2ac and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Attempts 01–03 remediated (`reviews/C18/remediation-attempt-0{1..3}.md`); D044 and D045 recorded; T20 workload registered |\n| P05 | **Complete**: Codex phase attempt-01 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 5ce089b and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Integrated native checks for C16–C18, the C18 workload and 133/133 mutation probes on the P05 bundle |\n| C19 | **Complete** (generation 1): Codex attempt-06 scored 9 in all five dimensions; committed as 7fee9f9 and verified | D046 recorded; Harness engine startup and memory workloads registered |\n| C20 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034, then raised; Codex attempt-03 passed; committed as aa4d4cf and verified | Follow-ups remediated (`reviews/C20/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C21 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034, then raised; Codex attempt-03 passed; committed as 702cc54 and verified | Follow-ups remediated (`reviews/C21/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C22 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034, then raised; Codex attempt-04 passed; committed as 8985a00 and verified | Follow-ups remediated (`reviews/C22/follow-ups.md`) |\n| P06 | **Complete**: Codex phase attempt-05 scored 9/9/9/9/9; committed as 3dbb2ce and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Integrated native checks and workloads for C19–C22 and 182 mutation probes on the P06 bundle; attempts remediated (`reviews/P06/remediation-attempt-0*.md`) |\n| C23 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034, then raised; Codex attempt-05 passed; committed as ba9cd27 and verified | Follow-ups remediated (`reviews/C23/follow-ups.md`) |\n| C24 | **Complete** (generation 2): completed at 8/10 under D034, then raised; Codex attempt-02 passed; committed as 582ae06 and verified | Follow-ups remediated (`reviews/C24/follow-ups.md`) |\n| P07 | **Complete**: Codex phase attempt-04 scored 9/9/9/9/9; committed as 6a7253c2 and verified against the reviewed source fingerprint | Integrated native checks for C01–C24, every workload and the production footprint on the P07 bundle and tree, and 76 mutation probes; attempts remediated (`reviews/P07/remediation-attempt-0*.md`) |\n| C25–C26 | Owner’s open P08 release phase: C25 historical live qualification accepted at 8; C26 release/install gates remain open | Preserved C26 October signing/install records are historical; pushing current source does not publish a release |\n| C27 | **Reviewed** (P09, D058): Codex attempt-05 scored 9 in all five dimensions through the fresh-exec fallback (`reviews/C27/attempt-05/receipt.json`); controller receipt and ledger completion regenerate once C26 completes | Attempts 01–04 remediated (`reviews/C27/remediation-attempt-0{1..4}.md`); follow-ups in `reviews/C27/follow-ups.md` |\n| C28 | **Reviewed** (P09, D058): Codex attempt-09 scored 9 in all five dimensions through the fresh-exec fallback (`reviews/C28/attempt-09/receipt.json`); native acceptance C28-N01–N07 recorded on the prepared fixture bundle; controller receipt and ledger completion regenerate once C26 completes | Attempts 01–08 remediated (`reviews/C28/remediation-attempt-0{1..8}.md`); follow-up in `reviews/C28/follow-ups.md` |\n| C29 | **Accepted at 8, remediation active** (P09, D034/D058): fresh read-only Codex attempt-07 scored **9/9/9/8/8**, no blockers; schema/hash/input audit passed; receipt `reviews/C29/attempt-07/receipt.json`. Actual authorized Vulture first-run verification passed on L19 attempt-03; the former live blocker is closed | R1/E1: restore retained Gateway, rejected/fixed/stale verification and keyed Cancel native assertions. R2/E2: all first-run/add steps in both themes at 100%/200% with per-step keyboard traversal. Corrected Worf C43 native run passed all 24 behaviors and 48 rows; independent wizard coverage audit passed. Full-9 re-review pending. Failed generation preserved under P09/native-history; no assertions retired |\n| C30 | **Predecessor re-review pending** (P09, D058): historical attempt-09 scored **9/9/9/8/8** while C29’s live row was blocked. L19 has since passed; C29 now needs its restored native coverage and full-9 re-review before this chunk is re-reviewed | Raw historical verdict unchanged. Run the fresh mapped native checks and review after the predecessor reaches 9; `WORF-START-HERE.md` gives the current sequence |\n| C31 | **Predecessor re-review pending** (P09, D058): historical attempt-04 scored **9/9/9/8/8** while C29’s live row was blocked. L19 has since passed; C29 now needs its restored native coverage and full-9 re-review before this chunk is re-reviewed | Raw historical verdict unchanged. Run the fresh mapped native checks and review after the predecessor reaches 9; `WORF-START-HERE.md` gives the current sequence |\n| C32 | **Predecessor re-review pending** (P09, D058): historical attempt-20 scored **9/9/9/8/8** while C29’s live row was blocked. L19 has since passed; C29 now needs its restored native coverage and full-9 re-review before this chunk is re-reviewed | Raw historical verdict unchanged. Run the fresh mapped native checks and review after the predecessor reaches 9; `WORF-START-HERE.md` gives the current sequence |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
