{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json; p=\\\"docs/planning/reviews/C32/attempt-20/verdict-returned.json\\\"; from pathlib import Path; p=Path(p) if Path(p).exists() else Path(str(p).replace(\\\"verdict-returned.json\\\",\\\"verdict.json\\\")); r=json.load(open(p)); print(json.dumps({k:r.get(k) for k in [\\\"scores\\\",\\\"required_fixes\\\",\\\"blockers\\\",\\\"evidence_gaps\\\",\\\"limitations\\\"]},indent=2))'\n sed -n '180,242p' tools/p09/c31_transition_policy.py\n sed -n '175,270p' tools/p09/phase_inputs_c31_transition.py\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"scores\": {\n    \"architecture\": 9,\n    \"behavior\": 9,\n    \"authority_security\": 9,\n    \"validation\": 8,\n    \"overall\": 8\n  },\n  \"required_fixes\": [],\n  \"blockers\": [\n    \"B1 \\u2014 docs/planning/chunks/C32.md requires C31. C31 attempt-04 still has a hash-matched failing verdict and receipt (9/9/9/8/8), carrying C29's missing mandatory live verification; C29 and C30 also retain failing receipts. D058 permits work while C26 remains open but does not waive this prerequisite. Resolve the C29 live blocker and obtain passing predecessor reviews/completions before completing C32.\"\n  ],\n  \"evidence_gaps\": [\n    \"E1 \\u2014 docs/planning/evidence/C29/live/blocked.json still records the required read-only Vulture wizard verification as unrun because the approved designation permits scans rather than management verification. Closure requires authorized scope, the actual wizard verification, a redacted source-bound receipt, and predecessor re-review. C32's fixture and native evidence cannot substitute for this mandatory predecessor evidence.\"\n  ],\n  \"limitations\": [\n    \"Reconstructed all four supplied fingerprints. All 300 scoped file hashes matched and remained unchanged at the final check. Both 18,286-entry compiled-input inventories match the dependency digest; 18,284 current inputs matched, with two .env.example files deliberately left unread. All 16 final log hashes, native preparation/acceptance hashes, prepared executable, engine archive and bundled engine pins, 25 screenshot copies, and six frozen prototype hashes matched. Hash consistency does not independently authenticate execution or evidence authorship.\",\n    \"Independently passed both package-local TypeScript checks using Node 24.21.0 and tsc --noEmit --incremental false. All twelve lifecycle snapshots passed the production parseShellSnapshot validator.\",\n    \"Independent in-memory React/jsdom probes exercised the production Harness, store, parser and DesktopClient with scripted transport and network access disabled. Pending-to-returned recovery passed on both send paths with admitted and lost receipts, newer edits and remounts; a tenant A/B/A retirement retained the exact pending message as Not confirmed without resending. Attempt-19 R1 is resolved in the inspected source. Reused legacy panels and text helpers were stubbed; the tenant retirement was simulated through snapshots and remounts.\",\n    \"Retained logs report 585 frontend tests, the separate truth test, six ui_v2_harness tests, and passing Rust, host, controller, lint, bindings, notices and frontend-build checks. The retained core-fixtures.flake-1.log records runtime_changes::a_confirmation_that_outlives_its_review_applies_nothing failing while waiting for its review; the final full-suite retry passed on the same inventoried inputs. Full suites and builds were not independently rerun. Whole xtask check/test commands were not run, as disclosed.\",\n    \"Inspected C32-N01\\u2013N04, the native driver, observations and all thirteen AX trees; independently recomputed zero right-edge overflow at 900x600/200% in both themes and visually inspected two representative screenshots. Native acceptance was not independently rerun. Captures are fixture WebView self-captures, the Gateway is synthetic, and spoken VoiceOver was not recorded. This establishes no live or signed installed-release qualification.\",\n    \"C27/C28 passing verdicts and C29/C30/C31 failing verdicts match their manual receipt hashes. Canonical controller receipt regeneration remains pending after C26. Unrelated C26 and Academy work was excluded from substantive review while consumed input hashes were checked. No application source was changed, product endpoint called or credential accessed.\",\n    \"Atomic verdict persistence was denied by the read-only sandbox when creating verdict.json.tmp. No verdict file was written; the controller must store this returned JSON.\"\n  ]\n}\n    require(changed == proof['source_delta_since_first_seal'], 'driver amendment source delta drift')\n    native_paths = {'tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c31.py', 'tools/native-acceptance/test_administration_coverage.py'}\n    require(set(changed) <= native_paths | ADMIN_PATHS, 'driver continuation changed application or unrelated source')\n    def inventory(path):\n        return {name.strip(): value for value, name in (line.split(None, 1) for line in path.read_text().splitlines())}\n    before_path = root / proof['compiled_inputs_before']\n    after_path = root / proof['compiled_inputs_after']\n    require(sha(before_path) == proof['before_digest'] and sha(after_path) == proof['after_digest'] == current_digest,\n            'driver amendment compiled-input seal drift')\n    before, after = inventory(before_path), inventory(after_path)\n    input_delta = sorted(name for name in set(before) | set(after) if before.get(name) != after.get(name))\n    require(input_delta == proof['compiled_input_changes'] and set(input_delta) <= native_paths,\n            'reused G8 application has changed compiled application inputs')\n    driver = 'tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c31.py'\n    old_driver = root / prefix / 'original-acceptance_c31.py'\n    require(sha(old_driver) == old[driver]['sha256'], 'old driver snapshot does not match first seal')\n    def normalized(path):\n        tree = ast.parse(path.read_text())\n        for node in tree.body:\n            if isinstance(node, ast.FunctionDef) and node.name == 'gateway_key_checks':\n                node.body = [ast.Pass()]\n        return ast.dump(tree, include_attributes=False)\n    require(normalized(old_driver) == normalized(root / driver), 'runtime change exceeds the Gateway key-check function')\n    callers = set()\n    for path in (root / 'tools/native-acceptance').glob('*.py'):\n        if path.name.startswith('test_'):\n            continue\n        tree = ast.parse(path.read_text())\n        if any(isinstance(n, ast.Call) and ((isinstance(n.func, ast.Name) and n.func.id == 'gateway_key_checks')\n                   or (isinstance(n.func, ast.Attribute) and n.func.attr == 'gateway_key_checks')) for n in ast.walk(tree)):\n            callers.add(str(path.relative_to(root)))\n    require(callers == {'tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c31.py', 'tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c39.py'},\n            'changed helper has additional runtime callers')\n    prep_path = root / 'docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-prepare.json'\n    build_path = root / 'docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-build-inputs.json'\n    require(sha(prep_path) == proof['prepare_sha256'] and sha(build_path) == proof['build_record_sha256'],\n            'original actual G8 preparation/build record changed')\n    prep = read(prep_path)\n    require(sha(root / prep['bundle'] / 'Contents/MacOS/prisma-airs-desktop-v2') == prep['executable_sha256'] == proof['executable_sha256'],\n            'G8 application executable changed')\n    entries = []\n    bundle = root / prep['bundle']\n    for path in sorted(bundle.rglob('*')):\n        if path.is_dir() and not path.is_symlink():\n            continue\n        if path.is_symlink():\n            mode, value = 'symlink', hashlib.sha256(os.readlink(path).encode()).hexdigest()\n        else:\n            mode, value = ('100755' if path.stat().st_mode & 0o111 else '100644'), sha(path)\n        entries.append(f'{path.relative_to(bundle)}\\0{mode}\\0{value}\\n')\n    require(hashlib.sha256(''.join(entries).encode()).hexdigest() == prep['bundle_sha256'] == proof['bundle_sha256'],\n            'complete G8 bundle changed')\n    require(len(proof['completed_native_steps']) == 10, 'wrong retained G8 step count')\n    for item in proof['completed_native_steps']:\n        for key in ['record', 'execution', 'log']:\n            require(sha(root / item[key]) == item[key + '_sha256'], 'retained G8 evidence changed: ' + item[key])\n        execution = read(root / item['execution'])\n        require(execution['driver_subject'] == item['subject'] and item['subject'] not in ['C31', 'C39', 'C44']\n                and execution['required_check_errors'] == [] and execution['executable_sha256'] == proof['executable_sha256'],\n                'invalid retained G8 native step')\n        require(sha(root / 'tools/native-acceptance' / ('acceptance_' + item['subject'].lower() + '.py')) == execution['driver_sha256'],\n                'retained native driver changed')\n    return {'record': str(proof_path.relative_to(root)), 'sha256': sha(proof_path),\n    return members\n\n\ndef native_build(root, prepared):\n    \"\"\"The current fixture build's actual before/after compiled-input seal.\"\"\"\n    path = root / 'docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-build-inputs.json'\n    build = read(path)\n    require(build['schema'] == 'airs-v2/p09-native-build-inputs/1', 'native build-input schema mismatch')\n    require(re.fullmatch(r'[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*', build['generation']) is not None,\n            'invalid native generation')\n    prefix = 'docs/planning/evidence/P09/preparations/' + build['generation'] + '/'\n    require(build['prepare'] == 'docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-prepare.json'\n            and build['command']['log'] == prefix + 'native-prepare.log'\n            and build['command']['cwd'] == str(root)\n            and build['command']['argv'] == ['cargo', 'run', '--locked', '-p', 'xtask', '--', 'native-prepare',\n                                            '--phase', 'P09', '--target', 'aarch64-apple-darwin', '--features', 'test-fixtures'],\n            'native build command/path mismatch')\n    require(build['worktree_diff'] == prefix + 'fixture-remediation.diff'\n            and sha(root / build['worktree_diff']) == build['worktree_diff_sha256'], 'native source-diff provenance mismatch')\n    require(build['prepare_sha256'] == sha(root / build['prepare'])\n            and build['executable_sha256'] == prepared['executable_sha256']\n            and build['bundle_sha256'] == prepared['bundle_sha256'], 'native build/preparation binding mismatch')\n    require(build['command']['exit'] == 0 and sha(root / build['command']['log']) == build['command']['log_sha256'],\n            'native build command failed or log changed')\n    value = build['inputs']\n    require(value['procedure'] == 'docs/planning/evidence/P09/runs/hash-inputs.sh'\n            and value['before_inventory'] == prefix + 'inputs-before.sha256'\n            and value['after_inventory'] == prefix + 'inputs-after.sha256', 'native inventory paths mismatch')\n    procedure = root / value['procedure']\n    require(sha(procedure) == value['procedure_sha256'], 'native build inventory procedure drift')\n    require(value['before_digest'] == value['after_digest'] == sha(root / value['before_inventory'])\n            == sha(root / value['after_inventory']), 'native build inputs changed')\n    require(value['unchanged'] is True and value['members'] == len((root / value['before_inventory']).read_text().splitlines())\n            and value['members'] > 0, 'native build inventory declaration mismatch')\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory(prefix='p09-native-inputs-') as scratch:\n        current = subprocess.check_output(['/bin/bash', str(procedure), str(root), str(Path(scratch) / 'inputs.sha256')], text=True).strip()\n    amendment = None\n    if current != value['before_digest']:\n        amendment = verify_driver_amendment(root, current)\n    return {'record': str(path.relative_to(root)), 'sha256': sha(path),\n            'generation': build['generation'], 'input_digest': current,\n            'original_build_input_digest': value['before_digest'], 'driver_amendment': amendment}\n\n\ndef verify_native(root):\n    controller = root / 'docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-controller'\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(controller))\n    from native_requirements import load_requirements, assess_record\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(root / 'tools/native-acceptance'))\n    import wizard_coverage\n    phase = root / 'docs/planning/evidence/P09'\n    prepared = read(phase / 'native-prepare.json')\n    require(prepared['subject'] == 'P09' and prepared['features'] == ['test-fixtures']\n            and prepared['target'] == 'aarch64-apple-darwin', 'wrong prepared subject/features/target')\n    executable = root / prepared['bundle'] / 'Contents/MacOS/prisma-airs-desktop-v2'\n    require(sha(executable) == prepared['executable_sha256'], 'prepared executable drift')\n    build = native_build(root, prepared)\n    records = []\n    for subject, required in sorted(load_requirements(root).items()):\n        directory = phase if subject == 'C44' else phase / 'native/cumulative' / subject\n        path = directory / 'native-acceptance.json'\n        record, execution = read(path), read(directory / 'execution.json')\n        require(record['subject'] == subject, subject + ': wrong record subject')\n        ids = [check['id'] for check in record['checks']]\n        require(len(ids) == len(set(ids)), subject + ': duplicate native check IDs')\n        require(sha(directory / 'native-prepare.json') == sha(phase / 'native-prepare.json'), subject + ': preparation mismatch')\n        errors, carried = assess_record(record, root, prepared['executable_sha256'], required)\n        require(not errors, subject + ': required native checks fail: ' + str(errors))\n        allowed_carried = {'C24': {'C24-N06'}, 'C31': {'C31-N01', 'C31-N04'}}\n        require(set(carried) <= allowed_carried.get(subject, set()), subject + ': unapproved superseded raw check')\n        require(execution['driver_return_code'] == 0 or (execution['driver_return_code'] == 1 and bool(carried)),\n                subject + ': unexplained driver exit')\n        require(execution['schema'] == 'airs-v2/p09-native-execution/1'\n                and execution['source_root'] == str(root)\n                and execution['driver_subject'] == subject and execution['phase'] == 'P09'\n                and execution['executable_sha256'] == prepared['executable_sha256']\n                and execution['raw_record_sha256'] == sha(path)\n                and execution['required_check_errors'] == errors and execution['superseded_raw_checks'] == carried,\n                subject + ': execution binding mismatch')\n        for field, source in [('controller_sha256', controller / 'run-p09-native.py'),\n                              ('requirements_sha256', controller / 'native_requirements.py'),\n                              ('driver_sha256', root / 'tools/native-acceptance' / ('acceptance_' + subject.lower() + '.py'))]:\n            require(execution[field] == sha(source), subject + ': execution source drift: ' + field)\n        require(subprocess.run(['git', 'merge-base', '--is-ancestor', execution['source_head'], 'HEAD'],\n                               cwd=root, capture_output=True).returncode == 0, subject + ': native source is not an integrated ancestor')\n        if subject == 'C43':\n            errors = wizard_coverage.problems(read(directory / 'native/observations.json')['observations'], root)\n            require(not errors, 'C43 retained coverage: ' + str(errors))\n        records.append({'subject': subject, 'record': str(path.relative_to(root)), 'sha256': sha(path),\n                        'started_utc': execution['started_utc'], 'finished_utc': execution['finished_utc'],\n                        'execution': str((directory / 'execution.json').relative_to(root)),\n                        'execution_sha256': sha(directory / 'execution.json'),\n                        'required_targets': sorted(required), 'superseded_raw_checks': carried,\n                        'executable_sha256': prepared['executable_sha256']})\n    ordered = sorted(records, key=lambda record: datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(record['started_utc']))\n    require([record['subject'] for record in ordered[:2]] == ['C36', 'C43'] and ordered[-1]['subject'] == 'C44',\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' tools/p09/c31_transition_policy.py\n sed -n '1,150p' docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-controller/native_requirements.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,180p' tools/p09/c31_transition_policy.py\n sed -n '1,150p' docs/planning/evidence/P09/native-controller/native_requirements.py\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Explicit C31-only transition from G7; historical qualification is never current.\n\nOriginal owner_closure_policy.py and all raw reviews remain immutable. The\ntransition manifest is sealed only after both declared fixes and preflight.\n\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nimport owner_closure_policy as baseline\nimport phase_inputs as original\n\nPREFIX = 'docs/planning/evidence/P09/c31-transition-20261102/'\nTRANSITION_RECORD = 'transition-final-01.json'\nBASE_HEAD = 'e825c2f69cbcd19387142b80481faaad84690a07'\nBASE_DIGEST = 'e441459dde8a4b13403f16f16e5abf100636421ff827f9955f37740500bbdc50'\nOWNER_SCORE = 'docs/planning/C30-owner-score-override-2026-11-02.md'\nOWNER_SHA = 'c150ebb6a35d8b1bdb6965a5780b96b88f393ed2994cdd3a11da2b4d20bd1a5e'\nFIX_PATHS = {\n    'crates/desktop-core/src/lib.rs',\n    'crates/desktop-core/src/presentation.rs',\n    'apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/native_confirmation.rs',\n    'tools/native-acceptance/mgmt_server.py',\n    'crates/desktop-core/src/authority.rs',\n    'crates/desktop-core/src/authority/change_domain.rs',\n    'crates/desktop-core/src/delivery.rs',\n    'crates/desktop-host/src/lib.rs',\n    'apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs',\n    'apps/desktop/src-tauri/Cargo.toml',\n    'crates/desktop-host/Cargo.toml',\n    'crates/desktop-host/tests/renderer_review_lifecycle.rs',\n    'apps/desktop/src-tauri/tests/renderer_review_lifecycle.rs',\n    'tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c31.py',\n    'tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c39.py',\n    'tools/native-acceptance/legacy_assertions.py',\n    'tools/native-acceptance/administration_coverage.py',\n    'tools/native-acceptance/test_administration_coverage.py',\n}\nADMIN_PATHS = {\n    '.gitattributes',\n    'docs/planning/C31-conditional-owner-override-2026-11-02.md',\n    'tools/p09/c31_owner_completion.py',\n    'tools/p09/test_c31_owner_completion.py',\n    'tools/p09/c31_transition_policy.py',\n    'tools/p09/phase_inputs_c31_transition.py',\n    'tools/p09/phase_packet_c31_transition.py',\n    'tools/p09/make-c31-transition-packet.py',\n    'tools/p09/audit-c31-transition-review.py',\n    'tools/p09/make-phase-packet-c31-transition.py',\n    'tools/p09/audit-phase-review-c31-transition.py',\n    'tools/p09/seal-c31-transition.py',\n    'tools/p09/test_c31_transition.py',\n    'tools/p09/audit-p09-checks-c31-transition.py',\n    'tools/p09/README.md',\n}\n\n\ndef digest(value):\n    return hashlib.sha256((json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':')) + '\\n').encode()).hexdigest()\n\n\ndef verify_transition(root):\n    from phase_packet_owner_closure import source_inventory\n    root = Path(root).resolve()\n    require, read, sha = original.require, original.read, original.sha\n    old = read(root / PREFIX / 'baseline-source.json')\n    require(old['head'] == BASE_HEAD and digest(old['files']) == old['digest'] == BASE_DIGEST,\n            'C31 transition baseline changed')\n    seal_path = root / PREFIX / TRANSITION_RECORD\n    seal = read(seal_path)\n    require(seal['baseline_head'] == BASE_HEAD and seal['baseline_digest'] == BASE_DIGEST,\n            'wrong transition baseline')\n    require(subprocess.run(['git', 'merge-base', '--is-ancestor', BASE_HEAD, 'HEAD'],\n                           cwd=root, capture_output=True).returncode == 0, 'baseline not integrated')\n    current = source_inventory(root)\n    changed = {name: {'before': old['files'].get(name), 'after': current.get(name)}\n               for name in sorted(set(old['files']) | set(current))\n               if old['files'].get(name) != current.get(name)}\n    require(changed == seal['source_delta'], 'current source differs from declared sealed C31 delta')\n    require(set(changed) <= FIX_PATHS | ADMIN_PATHS, 'undeclared non-C31 source change')\n    require(digest(current) == seal['current_source_digest'], 'current full source digest mismatch')\n    commit_paths = set()\n    require(len(seal['fix_commits']) >= 2, 'both collaborator fixes must be declared')\n    for commit in seal['fix_commits']:\n        require(subprocess.run(['git', 'merge-base', '--is-ancestor', commit, 'HEAD'],\n                               cwd=root, capture_output=True).returncode == 0, 'fix commit not integrated')\n        names = subprocess.check_output(['git', 'diff-tree', '--no-commit-id', '--name-only', '-r', commit],\n                                        cwd=root, text=True).splitlines()\n        require(all(name in FIX_PATHS or name.startswith('docs/planning/evidence/C31/remediation-attempt-05/') for name in names), 'fix commit changes unrelated source')\n        commit_paths.update(names)\n    require(set(changed) & FIX_PATHS <= commit_paths, 'production/driver delta lacks declared fix commit')\n    for item in seal['focused_results']:\n        focused = read(root / item['record'])\n        require(focused['exit'] == 0 and bool(focused['command']), 'focused command did not pass')\n        if 'log' in focused:\n            require(sha(root / focused['log']) == focused['log_sha256'], 'focused result log changed')\n        require(item['exit'] == 0 and sha(root / item['record']) == item['sha256'],\n                'focused preflight result missing/changed')\n    require(bool(seal['focused_results']), 'no focused preflight results')\n    require(sha(root / OWNER_SCORE) == OWNER_SHA, 'owner all-nine decision changed')\n    return {'record': PREFIX + TRANSITION_RECORD, 'sha256': sha(seal_path),\n            'baseline_head': BASE_HEAD, 'baseline_source_digest': BASE_DIGEST,\n            'current_source_digest': digest(current), 'changed_paths': sorted(changed),\n            'fix_commits': seal['fix_commits'], 'standing': 'C31-only production and native-driver remediation plus explicit administrative provenance; current qualification required'}\n\n\ndef verify_c30_owner_closure(root):\n    root = Path(root).resolve()\n    require, read, sha = original.require, original.read, original.sha\n    for name, expected in baseline.PINNED.items():\n        require(sha(root / name) == expected, 'historical C30 record changed: ' + name)\n    latest, verdict = original.latest_verdict(root, 'C30')\n    require(latest == root / baseline.ATTEMPT / 'verdict-returned.json', 'C30 has unexpected later review')\n    require(verdict['scores'] == baseline.SCORES and verdict['recommendation'] == 'fail', 'raw C30 verdict changed')\n    transition = verify_transition(root)\n    result = {'subject': 'C30', 'owner_closed': True, 'scores': verdict['scores'],\n              'recommendation': 'fail', 'full_gate_pass': False,\n              'owner_scores': {key: 9 for key in baseline.SCORES},\n              'owner_decision': OWNER_SCORE, 'owner_decision_sha256': OWNER_SHA,\n              'transition': transition,\n              'standing': 'Owner all-nine C30 standing continues across declared unrelated C31 delta; raw independent 9/9/9/8/8 remains historical. No C30 requalification or independent passing score claimed.'}\n    for key, name in [('record', 'verdict-returned.json'), ('request', 'request.json'),\n                      ('receipt', 'receipt.json'), ('audit', 'post-review-audit.json')]:\n        result[key] = baseline.ATTEMPT + '/' + name\n        result['sha256' if key == 'record' else key + '_sha256'] = sha(root / result[key])\n    return result\n\n\ndef historical_c29(root):\n    root = Path(root)\n    require, read, sha = original.require, original.read, original.sha\n    path, verdict = original.latest_verdict(root, 'C29')\n    require(verdict['attempt_id'] == 'attempt-10', 'unexpected C29 generation')\n    original.full_gate(verdict)\n    item = {'subject': 'C29', 'scores': verdict['scores'], 'recommendation': verdict['recommendation'],\n            'standing': 'Historical actual full-nine G7 review; shared authority file changes are declared C31-only delta, inspected by new C31 and cumulative P09 reviews. No current-source-equivalence claim.'}\n    # These committed audit artifacts remain byte-identical to the baseline.\n    for key, name in [('record', 'verdict-returned.json'), ('request', 'request.json'),\n                      ('receipt', 'receipt.json'), ('audit', 'post-review-audit.json')]:\n        rel = str((path.parent / name).relative_to(root))\n        old = subprocess.check_output(['git', 'show', BASE_HEAD + ':' + rel], cwd=root)\n        require(hashlib.sha256(old).hexdigest() == sha(root / rel), 'historical C29 record changed')\n        item[key] = rel\n        item['sha256' if key == 'record' else key + '_sha256'] = sha(root / rel)\n    require(read(path.parent / 'post-review-audit.json')['full_gate_pass'] is True, 'C29 original audit not passing')\n    return item\n\n\ndef historical_performance(root):\n    \"\"\"Retain historical performance honestly; owner explicitly forbids new C30 work.\"\"\"\n    root = Path(root)\n    rel = 'docs/planning/evidence/P09/workload-perf-C30.json'\n    old = subprocess.check_output(['git', 'show', BASE_HEAD + ':' + rel], cwd=root)\n    original.require(hashlib.sha256(old).hexdigest() == original.sha(root / rel), 'historical C30 performance changed')\n    return {'record': rel, 'sha256': original.sha(root / rel), 'current_qualification': False,\n            'standing': 'Historical G7 measurement retained under owner C30 closure; not a measurement of current C31 application bytes; no new C30 scenario or timing run authorized.'}\n\n\ndef verify_driver_amendment(root, current_digest):\n    \"\"\"Explicit same-G8 application continuation; never relabel historical runs.\"\"\"\n    import ast\n    import os\n    from phase_packet_owner_closure import source_inventory\n    root = Path(root)\n    require, read, sha = original.require, original.read, original.sha\n    prefix = PREFIX + 'driver-amendment-01/'\n    proof_path = root / prefix / 'equivalence.json'\n    proof = read(proof_path)\n    old_seal = root / PREFIX / 'transition.json'\n    require(sha(old_seal) == proof['original_transition_sha256'] == '39a2fd816437d55fbc163598a4b09f1dcb8f682c7acbe2f57cd1df4f7c070d4d', 'first source seal changed')\n    old = read(root / PREFIX / 'baseline-source.json')['files'].copy()\n    for name, value in read(old_seal)['source_delta'].items():\n        if value['after'] is None:\n            old.pop(name, None)\n        else:\n            old[name] = value['after']\n    current = source_inventory(root)\n    changed = {name: {'before': old.get(name), 'after': current.get(name)}\n               for name in sorted(set(old) | set(current)) if old.get(name) != current.get(name)}\n    require(changed == proof['source_delta_since_first_seal'], 'driver amendment source delta drift')\n\"\"\"Read the C44 gate's existing assertion map without changing its requirements.\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport re\nimport runpy\n\n\ndef load_requirements(root):\n    manifest = json.loads((root / 'docs/architecture/native-checks.json').read_text())['chunks']\n    data = runpy.run_path(str(root / 'tools/native-acceptance/legacy_assertions.py'))\n    assertions = data['ASSERTIONS']\n    legacy_ids = {c['id'] for chunk, checks in manifest.items()\n                  if re.fullmatch(r'C(0[1-9]|1\\d|2\\d|3[0-3])', chunk) for c in checks}\n    assert legacy_ids == set(assertions), 'legacy map differs from the full manifest'\n    targets = {t for kind, ts, _ in assertions.values()\n               if kind in (data['X'], data['S'], data['P']) for t in ts}\n    self_run = {lid.split('-')[0] for lid, (kind, _, _) in assertions.items() if kind == data['S']}\n    required = {chunk: {t for t in targets if t.startswith(chunk + '-')} for chunk in self_run}\n    # Some legacy ids are carried by a different self-run driver. Only drivers with actual targets run;\n    # the union check below still requires every mapped target to be covered.\n    required = {chunk: checks for chunk, checks in required.items() if checks}\n    for chunk in [f'C{i}' for i in range(35, 45)]:\n        required[chunk] = {c['id'] for c in manifest[chunk]}\n    assert all(required.values()), 'empty required native check set'\n    assert targets <= set().union(*required.values()), 'mapped native target has no driver'\n    return required\n\n\ndef assess_record(record, root, executable_sha256, required):\n    errors = []\n    if record.get('app', {}).get('executable_sha256') != executable_sha256:\n        errors.append('stale executable')\n    checks = {c['id']: c for c in record.get('checks', [])}\n    for cid in sorted(required):\n        check = checks.get(cid)\n        if check is None:\n            errors.append(cid + ' missing')\n        elif check['result'] != 'pass':\n            errors.append(cid + ' ' + check['result'])\n        else:\n            errors.extend(cid + ' missing evidence: ' + e for e in check['evidence'] if not (root / e).exists())\n    carried_elsewhere = [cid for cid, c in checks.items() if cid not in required and c['result'] != 'pass']\n    return errors, carried_elsewhere\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
