tes/desktop-core/tests/harness_identity_history |\n| C20-N07 | After a relaunch, a saved conversation opens as a list of its messages and continues in a new engine with its history restored (the Gateway … | a saved conversation continues after a relaunch: crates/desktop-core/tests/harness_identity_history |\n| C20-N08 | Export saves the opened conversation's transcript (Markdown) through the save sheet, with no key, token or replay; Delete asks first, then r… | export and delete of a saved conversation: harness_identity_history and harness.test.tsx (the v2 history panel) |\n| C20-N09 | The credential choice is a labelled radio group, Saved conversations is a heading with a named list, and Sign in is reached by Tab from the … | the credential choice and history list roles: harness.test.tsx (the v2 panels) |\n| C20-N11 | An unreadable saved conversation (a record that does not open with its workspace's key) is deleted only when confirmed, by keyboard: activat… | an unreadable record deleted only when confirmed: harness_identity_history and harness.test.tsx |\n| C20-N12 | Offline (T23): relaunched with the synthetic Gateway and identity provider stopped, the Harness lists the last chosen workspace's history fr… | offline history: crates/desktop-core/tests/harness_identity_history |\n| C21-N01 | The project folder is chosen in the native 'Choose project folder' sheet (the production NSOpenPanel) and shown with its path, read-only; a … | the project folder sheet and a refused system folder: crates/desktop-core/tests/harness_tools and harness.test.tsx |\n| C21-N04 | Allowing changes is a new binding: the running conversation ends and its engine is reaped. In the next conversation an allowed command write… | allowing changes rebinds the conversation: crates/desktop-core/tests/harness_tools |\n| C21-N05 | A proposed change is staged, never applied: it is listed under Proposed changes and no management write is sent; Review opens it in Administ… | a proposed change staged into Administration's review: crates/desktop-core/tests/harness_tools |\n| C21-N06 | Forged or unknown tool calls run nothing: an unknown tool, a credential-bearing argument and a Gateway change proposal are each answered as … | forged or unknown tool calls run nothing: crates/desktop-core/tests/harness_tools |\n| C21-N09 | Offline and reconnecting (T23): with a command waiting for its approval and a proposal open in review, the app quits and relaunches with the… | offline with a waiting approval: crates/desktop-core/tests/harness_tools |\n| C22-N02 | A conversation gives the engine the server with its bearer in memory and its startup reads ready; the model's MCP tool call waits for the op… | an MCP tool call waits for the operator: crates/desktop-core/tests/workspace_mcp |\n| C22-N03 | Once the MCP token is inside its renewal margin, the next message renews it (one refresh), stops the engine and starts a new one that restor… | MCP token renewal: crates/desktop-core/tests/workspace_mcp |\n| C22-N04 | An expired MCP sign-in (its renewal refused) keeps inference: the engine gets the signed-out placeholder, the server reads not signed in, it… | an expired MCP sign-in keeps inference: crates/desktop-core/tests/workspace_mcp |\n| C22-N05 | Signing out of a server retires the running conversation, reaps its engine, deletes its Keychain item and revokes both tokens; signing in ag… | signing out of a server retires the conversation: crates/desktop-core/tests/workspace_mcp |\n| C30-N01 | With a Harness conversation waiting for the operator's approval (the real pinned engine against the synthetic Gateway), switching tenants th… | the tenant-switch guard with a Harness decision waiting: crates/desktop-core/tests/ui_v2_inbox and the shell's switch-guard tests (apps/desktop/src/v2) |\n| C31-N03 | The staged Runtime key rotation: 'Issue additional key…' reviewed with CREATE and confirmed natively issues one key and shows 'Additional ke… | the staged Runtime key rotation and the host secret sheet: crates/desktop-core/tests/runtime_changes and the host's secret-sheet tests (not on C39's board) |\n\n# C38 — Harness\n\nPhase: P09 (re-cut, D059). Status: planned. Required predecessor: C37.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe screen matches its prototype board side by side at 1440×900 in light and dark with real core data, as the owner approved from the chunk's composites, and passes its gate at 8.\n\n## The board\n\nR2App `start=harness` with `convo` blocks, mcp, keys. The frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is the specification; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md` states the bar.\n\n## Regions to port\n\nthe title band; a 244px conversation rail; the transcript with a 46px composer; a 350px Decisions aside; setup (project, sign-in, MCP) as v2 components, not the legacy panels; all C32 behaviour (named sends, Not confirmed, contextual restart) unchanged.\n\n## Core it reads\n\n`ShellSnapshot.harness`; intents `startHarness`, `sendHarness`, `decideHarnessApproval`, `endHarness`, `openHarnessHistory`, `resumeHarness`, project/sign-in/MCP intents. No new core capability unless named here; v2 components import no legacy feature view.\n\n## Parity\n\nComposites at `docs/planning/evidence/C38/parity/<board>-<theme>.png` (prototype left, app right) with `notes.md` listing accessibility deviations; the owner's approval is recorded there before the gate.\n\n## Gate\n\nRebuild, native acceptance (C38-N01 three-column regions and a decision in the aside; C38-N02 keyboard, ring, 900×600 at 200% both themes), the full desktop-core fixture suite and the Codex review; accepted at 8 (D032/D034), raised to 9 in C44.\n\n## Tests\n\n`ui_v2_harness_port`; Vitest `v2/harness/harness.test.tsx` (existing suite kept green).\n# C44 — Legacy shell removal, P09 closure\n\nPhase: P09 (re-cut, D059). Status: planned. Required predecessor: C43.\n\nD060 (2026-10-31): the alpha import (C23's Import from v1 destination, view, wizard box and first-run frame) is removed in this chunk; C23's native checks are retired and the cumulative set drops `acceptance_c23.py`.\n\n## Outcome\n\nThe screen matches its prototype board side by side at 1440×900 in light and dark with real core data, as the owner approved from the chunk's composites, and passes its gate at 8.\n\n## The board\n\n—. The frozen prototype under `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` is the specification; `docs/planning/p09-recut.md` states the bar.\n\n## Regions to port\n\nmap every assertion in the legacy native acceptance scripts to its replacement driver and native-check id (`legacy-script-map.md` under the chunk evidence); remove the legacy shell, its feature-view switch, the `ui_variant` flag, the legacy feature components no v2 screen imports, and the legacy scripts, in one commit on a branch merged after review; cumulative native acceptance of every destination and the whole-app screenshot set; every C28–C43 chunk accepted at 8 raised to 9; the P09 phase review at 9 (the C29 live Vulture row must have run).\n\n## Core it reads\n\n—. No new core capability unless named here; v2 components import no legacy feature view.\n\n## Parity\n\nComposites at `docs/planning/evidence/C44/parity/<board>-<theme>.png` (prototype left, app right) with `notes.md` listing accessibility deviations; the owner's approval is recorded there before the gate.\n\n## Gate\n\nRebuild, native acceptance (C44-N01 cumulative acceptance of every destination), the full desktop-core fixture suite and the Codex review; accepted at 8 (D032/D034), raised to 9 in C44.\n\n## Tests\n\n`ui_v2_closure`.\n\n## The workspace key on the one presentation\n\nThe legacy AI Gateway view's Playground held the form that saved a workspace's inference key (C18); with that view gone, the first-run wizard's tenant step saves the key and the Gateway card's Workspaces tab holds the same form for the chosen workspace (`data-slot=\"gateway-workspace-key\"`: Inference endpoint, Workspace inference key, Save or Replace workspace key, Remove workspace key; the key's Keychain state from the tenant's snapshot; the field is emptied as soon as the secret is sent). The Harness's missing-key text and the wizard's hint name that tab. Found by the cumulative run of the C38 driver, whose setup now saves the key there.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
